    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5037": {
      "title": "Federal Student Worker - Canteen Sales Ambassador",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Federal Student Worker - Canteen Sales Ambassador Federal Student Worker - Canteen Sales Ambassador No. 5037 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Dean-RocNation School Posted Oct 15, 2026 $17 per hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 per hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Dec 30, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary Canteen Sales Ambassadors support the day-to-day operation of the Canteen at the Brooklyn Campus. Ambassadors welcome and assist customers, operate the point-of-sale (POS) system, maintain an organized and inviting store environment, assist with inventory and online orders, and help create a positive experience for students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors. Key Responsibilities Welcome and assist customers with purchases, questions, and general inquiries. Operate the point-of-sale (POS) system to process sales and other transactions accurately. Provide friendly, professional customer service. Maintain a clean, organized, and welcoming Canteen environment. Restock merchandise and assist with inventory organization and labeling. Prepare and fulfill online sales orders. Assist with general Canteen operations and facility upkeep. Work collaboratively with other student ambassadors and Canteen staff. Represent the Canteen and university in a friendly and professional manner. Education Requirements: LIU students currently enrolled in an active degree program and are eligible for Federal Work Study during the period of employment. Training, Skills, Knowledge, Experience: A few qualities are important to success in this role, while the rest can be learned along the way. No prior training or experience is required, just bring your motivation! Important Qualities: Dependable and punctual. Friendly, positive, and professional attitude. Strong communication and customer service skills. Willingness to learn and work as part of a team. Ability to work independently when needed. Helpful skills and experience: Ability to learn and operate a POS system. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Previous retail, cashier, or customer service experience. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunities in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 3 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like Roc Nation Student Worker... #3459 Dean-RocNation School Federal Work Study Student Worker - Music Studio ... #5030 Dean-RocNation School Federal Work Study Student Worker - Kumble Theater... #5031 Dean-RocNation School © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
