    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4217": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice NTTA",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice NTTA Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice NTTA No. 4217 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Pharmacy Practice Posted Oct 15, 2026 $120,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Faculty Salary Range $120,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Oct 15, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary LIU Pharmacy invites applications for full-time, non-tenure\ntrack, Assistant/Associate Professor positions in the Division of Pharmacy\nPractice. Positions are open in inpatient general medicine and in ambulatory\ncare. The faculty will be responsible for precepting students in advanced\npharmacy practice experiences where students apply their pharmaceutical\nknowledge to a variety of disease states. The faculty’s practice site will be\none of the prestigious medical centers/hospitals/clinics within the five\nboroughs of New York City affiliated with the College of Pharmacy. Faculty\nresponsibilities also include didactic teaching and providing clinical services\nat the practice site and service at the College. Faculty members are expected\nto build a portfolio of scholarly work within their area of interest. Located in Downtown Brooklyn, in one of New York City’s\nmost diverse and thriving urban communities, LIU Pharmacy (The Arnold &\nMarie Schwartz College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences), one of the oldest\nschools of pharmacy in the nation, prepares students for successful careers in\nthe fields of pharmacy and health care. In addition to world-class faculty, a\nvibrant campus life and residence halls, the campus is home to the $45-million\nSteinberg Wellness Center, which features an NCAA-regulation swimming pool, a\n2,500-seat arena, state-of-the-art workout facilities and a rooftop track for\nstudents, faculty, staff, alumni, and the local community. Minimum Qualifications Candidates who are PGY1-trained or those without residency training may be considered if they possess significant comparable experience. PharmD degree with PGY 1 residency. PGY 2 residency training is preferred. Licensed in the State of New York or to be licensed within 180 days of employment at LIU. Interested individuals must submit a cover letter,\ncurriculum vitae, as well as a teaching philosophy and a summary of their\nscholarly interests via the LIU Employment Opportunities portal (available at:\nhttps://jobs.liu.edu/#/job_details/4217). Additionally, three letters of\nrecommendation must be emailed to Dr. Joseph Nathan, Chair of the Division of\nPharmacy Practice (joseph.nathan@liu.edu). Applications will be accepted until\nthe position is filled. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is\ncommitted to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified\ncandidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic\ncommunity. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without\nregard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation,\ngender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status,\nnational origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status,\nage, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or\nfederal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 4 Days Since Posted 3 Positions Available Faculty Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4949": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Post Doctoral Fellow Post Doctoral Fellow No. 4949 Long Island University Brookville, New York Veterinary Biomedical Sciences Posted Oct 15, 2026 $50,000-$55,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $50,000-$55,000 FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Jan 01, 2027 Job Description Position Summary A Postdoctoral Fellow in Molecular Virology is available in the laboratory of Prof. Dr. Maged\nHemida at the Long Island University College of Veterinary Medicine (LIU-CVM), New York,\nUSA. The successful candidate will join an interdisciplinary research program investigating virus-\nhost interactions and the molecular mechanisms of viral pathogenesis within the\nframework of the One Health concept. Ongoing projects focus on emerging and zoonotic\nviruses affecting both human and animal health, including studies on viral pathogenesis,\nhost immune responses, antiviral strategies, vaccine development, and computational\napproaches for infectious disease research. This position provides an excellent opportunity for a highly motivated scientist to develop\nan independent research portfolio while collaborating with multidisciplinary investigators\nin virology, immunology, molecular biology, veterinary medicine, and computational\nbiology. Primary Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Design, plan, and execute independent research projects in molecular virology and virus-\nhost interactions. Perform molecular cloning, plasmid construction, and recombinant DNA techniques. Express and purify recombinant proteins using bacterial and mammalian expression\nsystems. Maintain mammalian cell cultures and perform viral infection experiments under\nappropriate biosafety conditions. Conduct molecular and cellular biology techniques including: PCR, RT-PCR, quantitative real-time PCR (qPCR) Western blotting and immunoblotting Immunofluorescence assays (IFA) Confocal microscopy and fluorescence imaging Flow cytometry ELISA and immunological assays RNA interference (siRNA/shRNA) and gene silencing CRISPR/Cas-based genome editing (preferred) Viral titration assays (TCID 50 , plaque assays, focus-forming assays) Perform nucleic acid and protein extraction, purification, and quantitative analyses. Analyze experimental data using appropriate statistical and bioinformatics tools. Assist in next-generation sequencing (NGS) data analysis, transcriptomics, or viral\ngenomics when applicable. Maintain accurate laboratory records and ensure proper organization, storage, and\ndocumentation of research data. Prepare figures, reports, manuscripts, conference abstracts, and presentations. Participate in the preparation of grant applications and progress reports. Mentor graduate, DVM, undergraduate, and visiting research students. Assist in laboratory management, including ordering supplies, maintaining laboratory\nequipment, and ensuring compliance with institutional biosafety and laboratory safety\nregulations. Collaborate effectively with internal and external research partners. Required Qualifications\nApplicants should possess: A Ph.D. in Virology, Molecular Biology, Microbiology, Immunology, Cell Biology,\nBiotechnology, Veterinary Medicine, or a closely related discipline. A strong publication record in peer-reviewed scientific journals. Demonstrated expertise in molecular and cellular biology techniques. Hands-on experience with mammalian cell culture and molecular virology. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving abilities. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively to a collaborative research\nenvironment. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with experience in one or more of the following\nareas: Virus-host interaction studies Reverse genetics systems Emerging and zoonotic viruses Viral immunology Flow cytometry and advanced microscopy Confocal microscopy and live-cell imaging RNA sequencing and next-generation sequencing (NGS) Bioinformatics and computational biology Protein structural biology\nAI-assisted biological data analysis Multi-omics data integration Statistical programming using R, Python, or similar software Research Environment The Hemida Laboratory conducts cutting-edge research in molecular virology with\nemphasis on: Emerging and re-emerging viral diseases One Health approaches to infectious diseases Coronavirus biology Influenza and avian viral diseases Feline infectious diseases Viral evolution and genomics Host immune responses Vaccine development Antiviral discovery Artificial intelligence applications in infectious disease research The laboratory provides an interactive and collaborative research environment with\nopportunities to publish in high-impact journals, present at national and international\nconferences, develop grant-writing skills, and build an independent research career. Application Instructions Interested applicants should submit application through the link on this page:\nCover letter describing research interests and career goals\nCurrent Curriculum Vitae (CV)\nList of technical expertise\nComplete list of publications\nContact information for three professional references\nReview of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For additional information, please contact:Prof. Dr. Maged Hemida\nProfessor of Molecular Virology\nCollege of Veterinary Medicine\nLong Island University\nBrookville, New York, USA\nEmail: maged.hemida@liu.edu Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 4 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like Postdoctoral Fellow ... #4982 Veterinary Biomedical Sciences Administrative Assistant - Office of Academic Affa... #4995 Veterinary Biomedical Sciences © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5047": {
      "title": "3DEXPERIENCE Platform Research Engineer",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU 3DEXPERIENCE Platform Research Engineer 3DEXPERIENCE Platform Research Engineer No. 5047 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Digital Engineering and Artificial Intelligence Posted Oct 15, 2026 $85,000 - $90,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $85,000 - $90,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Jan 15, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary Long Island University (LIU) and Fortune 50 company Dassault Systèmes have forged a groundbreaking partnership to establish the world’s first 3DEXPERIENCE Education and Research Center of Excellence in Life Sciences. This center is dedicated to advancing pharmaceutical sciences, precision medicine, and healthcare in the digital era through impactful research. It brings together a multidisciplinary team of experts from LIU, renowned for their collaborative spirit and expertise across diverse fields such as engineering, pharmacology, data management, clinical trial oversight, artificial intelligence, machine learning , and clinical research involving diverse populations and settings. Key Responsibilities Define & implement the 3DEXPERIENCE Platform portfolio of offerings/apps and services. Manage the 3DEXPERIENCE Platform portfolio of offerings/apps and services. Work closely with students and faculty to ensure training on the various 3DEXPERIENCE Platform soft and hardware. Interface with Dassault Systèmes for any soft or hardware updates Challenges Ahead 3DEXPERIENCE Platform Manager will: Focus on technical aspects of software product management. Lead and manage 3DEXPERIENCE Online Platform apps from the inception to the retirement in order to maximize 3DEXPERIENCE platform business values. Responsibilities span beyond project/app management and include the overall 3DEXPERIENCE dissemination strategy within students, faculty and state stakeholders. Use his/her rich experience of product development in discreet manufacturing industry, common customer needs/expectation and design processes, specifically related to the ongoing challenges, solutions, best practices and latest trends related to collaboration with the whole eco system, information creation and management. Will also use experience of software and social platforms, and SaaS trends on the market, to clearly define the product portfolio, capabilities, functionality, create and prioritize use cases and requirements. Analyze the market and work closely with the 3DEXPERIENCE end-users (companies for training and continuing education), in order to define and manage customer workflows and use cases to be used for gap definition and development prioritization. Will work closely with other teams and stake holders inside Dassault Systèmes in order to successfully plan, develop and deliver to market portfolio of Online CAD offerings. This include collaboration and synchronize activates with DS Platform Team, and all other brands (CATIA, BIOVIA, etc.), Product Definition, UX, R&D and QA teams. Required Qualifications: This position offers excellent opportunities for technical career advancement and leadership by contributing to the development of algorithms and software in the aforementioned areas. The ideal candidate will have experience in simulation software development and proficiency in modern programming techniques. Additionally, a strong understanding of the following 3DEXPERIENCE Solutions is essential: 3DEXCITE – High Precision Rendering and Interactive Actions (AR / VR) BIOVIA – Molecular modeling  • CATIA – Design Engineering and System Engineering CATIA - Architecture and Civil Engineering • DELMIA – Digital Manufacturing and Production ENOVIA – Collaborative Innovation and Project Management SIMULIA - Advanced Realistic Simulation SOLIDWORKS – 3D Designer for Product Design Candidates must have an earned a Master degree before the start date of the position in one of the following fields: Computational Sciences, Engineering, or a related field. Candidates with interest in research have the potential to prepare a PhD in the field of their choice enabling a career evolution as a faculty in LIU. The position will be housed in the Department of 3DS/FabLab/Accelerator facilities under the School of Engineering, AI and Computer Sciences. Candidates must have an earned a Master degree before the start date of the position in one of the following fields: Computational Sciences, Engineering, or a related field. Candidates with interest in research have the potential to prepare a PhD in the field of their choice enabling a career evolution as a faculty in LIU. The position will be housed in the Department of 3DS/FabLab/Accelerator facilities under the School of Engineering, AI and Computer Sciences. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regards to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 4 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/3984": {
      "title": "Program Director and Assistant/Associate Professor, Physician Assistant Studies Program",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Program Director and Assistant/Associate Professor, Physician Assistant Studies Program Program Director and Assistant/Associate Professor, Physician Assistant Studies Program No. 3984 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Physician Assistant Program Posted Oct 14, 2026 $130,000 - $145,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Faculty Salary Range $130,000 - $145,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Feb 01, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary Long Island University (LIU) invites dynamic healthcare and academic leaders to apply for the combined role of Program Director and Assistant/Associate Professor of Physician Assistant Studies within the School of Health Professions at LIU Brooklyn. The\nDepartment of Physician Assistant (PA) Studies in the School of Health\nProfessions is seeking a full-time, program director, non-tenure track\nassistant/associate professor in our Master of Science program. This is a nine-month\nfaculty position with a twelve-month administrative position requiring didactic\nand clinical teaching; student advisement, remediation, and retention;\nuniversity committee participation; and assessment evaluation as per ARC-PA and\nuniversity standards. About the Program The Long Island University PA Program is an intensive 28-month professional Master of Science course of study designed to shape the next generation of compassionate, highly skilled medical practitioners. Set in the vibrant urban campus environment of Downtown Brooklyn with robust clinical partnerships across the New York metropolitan area, our program combines rigorous didactic coursework, hands-on laboratory learning, and 15 months of premier clinical rotations. It holds a legacy as one of the oldest and most established PA programs in the New York City metropolitan area. The new Program Director and faculty member will champion an innovative curriculum that emphasizes evidence-based practice, interprofessional collaboration, and student-centered mentorship, all while shaping future leaders in the Physician Assistant profession. Key Responsibilities Teach didactic and\n     clinical year students: both lectures, laboratories and small group\n     learning Provide remediation\n     instruction to ensure student success Review and update PA\n     syllabi and curricula Work collaboratively\n     with members of the PA and university faculty/administration Advise students in both\n     didactic and clinical years Participate in clinical\n     site visits as needed Participate in student\n     recruitment and retention activities Promote the PA Program\n     and PA profession to potential students and community Participate in the\n     review, interviewing and selection of applicants for admission to the PA\n     Program Participate in ARC-PA\n     program assessment, data collection and analysis and preparation of\n     self-study reports Work collaboratively\n     with members of the PA and university faculty/administration Serve on Departmental,\n     School of Health Professions and University committees Minimum Qualifications NCCPA-certified Physician Assistant (PA-C) with current or emeritus NCCPA certification Current New York State PA license or eligibility for licensure in New York State Master’s degree or higher from an accredited physician assistant program Three years full-time higher education experience Teaching experience is required Demonstrated leadership, organizational, and administrative skills Excellent oral and written skills About LIU Brooklyn LIU Brooklyn campus enables\nstudents to realize their full potential as ethically grounded, intellectually\nvigorous, and socially responsible global citizens. The campus offers more\nprofessional programs in health care than any other campus in the New York\nmetropolitan area, including the Arnold and Marie Schwartz College of Pharmacy\n& Health Science, and The Harriet Rothkopf Heilbrunn School of Nursing. LIU\nBrooklyn is home to Kumble Theater for the Performing Arts, a dynamic\nperformance venue designed to nourish students’ artistic exploration, and\nDivision I sports teams. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending\nequal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute\nto the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages\napplications from all qualified individuals without regards to race, color,\nreligion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender\nidentity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity,\ncitizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other\nbasis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is\ncontingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 4 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Faculty Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
