    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5046": {
      "title": "FWS Student Worker - Front Desk Assistant",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU FWS Student Worker - Front Desk Assistant FWS Student Worker - Front Desk Assistant No. 5046 Long Island University Brookville, New York Counseling-Student Health Posted Oct 14, 2026 $17 per hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 per hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Jan 14, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary The Center for Healthy Living is seeking a friendly, dependable, and professional Work Study student to assist with front desk and administrative operations within the counseling center. The Front Desk Assistant serves as an initial point of contact for students visiting or contacting CHL and helps maintain a welcoming, confidential, and supportive environment. Responsibilities Greet and assist students who visit the Center for Healthy Living. Answer phones, respond to general inquiries, and direct students to appropriate staff or resources. Assist with scheduling and appointment-related administrative tasks. Provide students with general information about CHL counseling services and campus resources. Assist with routine administrative tasks, filing, data entry, copying, scanning, and other office duties. Maintain a clean, organized, and welcoming front desk area. Assist with outreach materials, events, and other CHL projects as needed. Follow all CHL policies regarding confidentiality, privacy, professional boundaries, and appropriate handling of student information. Minimum Qualifications Must be an LIU student eligible for Federal Work Study. Professional, friendly, and approachable demeanor. Strong communication and organizational skills. Dependable and able to work independently. Comfortable interacting with students, faculty, and staff. Ability to maintain confidentiality and demonstrate appropriate professional boundaries. Previous office, customer service, or administrative experience is helpful but not required. This position is located within the Center for Healthy Living Counseling Center at Post Hall and provides an opportunity to gain experience in a professional college counseling and student support environment. Important: This is a non-clinical position. The Work Study student will not provide counseling, clinical services, or clinical advice to students. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 5 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
