    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4995": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant - Office of Academic Affairs",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Administrative Assistant - Office of Academic Affairs Administrative Assistant - Office of Academic Affairs No. 4995 Long Island University Brookville, New York Veterinary Biomedical Sciences Posted Oct 07, 2026 $45,000 - $50,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $45,000 - $50,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Nov 26, 2026 Contact Please complete online application Job Description This is a full-time position. The ideal\ncandidate should be a self-motivated individual with solid work ethic who\ndemonstrates certain competencies including: Problem\n     solving Professionalism Adaptability Exceptional\n     attention to details and accuracy Strong organizational skills with an ability to\nprioritize and manage multiple task Ability to maintain confidentiality and maintain\ndiscretion. Strong interpersonal skills and a commitment to\nfostering an inclusive environment Excellent\nverbal and written communication skills Technology\nexperience and expertise, such as computers, spreadsheets, data management\nsystems, presentations, and word processing software programs, with proficiency\nin Microsoft Office, Outlook, Adobe Acrobat, and Online Conference software\nprograms.  Familiarity with eValue preferred Proficiency\n     in the use of spread sheets and databases, including Blackboard, Exam\n     Soft, and People Soft Ability to work independently and\ncollaboratively in a dynamic, fast-paced environment Willingness and ability to learn new, relevant\ntechnologies as they become available, such as those associated with artificial\nintelligence Duties and Responsibilities Provide high-level,\n     complex administrative support to ensure efficient, effective operation of\n     the Office of Academic Affairs. Assist with\n     coordination of activities of the team of staff within the Office of\n     Academic Affairs Assist with\n     data collection and management, such as those related to curriculum,\n     student, faculty, and accreditation as they pertain to academic affairs\n     responsibilities Organize and\n     maintain a variety of records, databases, files, and other documents\n     pertaining to the functions of the Office of Academic Affairs Provide\ncurrent and accurate information in support of the daily activities of the Office\nof Academic Affairs Plan\nand coordinate logistical and administrative support for meetings, events,\nspecialized activities, projects, and long-term initiatives Assist\nin resolving complex, highly sensitive, and confidential administrative matters,\nas requested Filter correspondence and compose responses on\nbehalf of the Office of Academic Affairs, including thank you notes,\nmemorandums, emails, etc. Answer phone calls and respond to non-routine\ninformation requests Work closely with students, other offices,\nstaff, faculty, and departments to facilitate smooth operations and foster a\ncollaborative environment, contributing to team objectives and morale Provide faculty members assistance with\nfunctions related to the Office of Academic Affairs, such as important software\nprograms Oversee coordination of high impact events, such\nas those related to the office. Coordinate with university offices for quality,\non-brand delivery of services, as needed, such as Academic Affairs, Students\nAffairs, HR, IT, Operations, and Marketing Ensure strict confidentiality is maintained on\nall matters Oversee and direct others Serve on College of Veterinary Medicine\ncommittees Requirements: Bachelor’s\n     degree or equivalent combination of education and experience Minimum of 3\n     years of administrative support experience, preferably in a college or\n     university setting Project\n     management experience preferred Previous\n     supervisory experience preferred An\n     employee in this position must complete all appropriate background checks\n     at the time of hire LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending\nequal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute\nto the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages\napplications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color,\nreligion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender\nidentity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity,\ncitizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other\nbasis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is\ncontingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 12 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like Postdoctoral Fellow ... #4982 Veterinary Biomedical Sciences Post Doctoral Fellow... #4949 Veterinary Biomedical Sciences © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
