    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4827": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Music Department",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Student Worker - Music Department Student Worker - Music Department No. 4827 Long Island University Brookville, New York Music Posted Oct 07, 2026 $17 per hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 per hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Apr 22, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Position Summary The Department of Music at Long Island University seeks responsible and dependable student workers to provide general support for departmental operations. This position is designed as a flexible, entry-level student employment role and may be utilized to support a variety of administrative, academic, and event-related needs within the Department of Music. Duties will be assigned based on departmental priorities, operational needs, and student availability. This position is open to currently enrolled Long Island University students. While music majors and students participating in departmental ensembles or programs are encouraged to apply, all eligible LIU students are welcome to be considered. Key Responsibilities Student workers may assist with a combination of the following duties: • Provide general administrative support, including filing, copying, data entry, and basic office organization • Assist faculty and staff with day-to-day departmental operations • Support rehearsals, concerts, recitals, and special events as needed • Help with setup and breakdown of classrooms, rehearsal spaces, and performance venues • Monitor practice rooms, studios, or departmental facilities when assigned • Assist with equipment, instrument, or music library organization • Serve as a point of contact for students, faculty, staff, and visitors, offering professional and courteous assistance • Perform other related duties as assigned to support the mission of the Required Qualifications • Must be a currently enrolled student at Long Island University • Strong organizational and time-management skills • Ability to follow instructions and work independently when needed • Dependable, punctual, and professional in conduct • Effective verbal and written communication skills • Ability to maintain confidentiality when handling sensitive information Preferred Qualifications (Not Required) • Interest in music, music education, music technology, or performing arts • Previous office, event, or customer service experience • Basic computer skills (e.g., email, word processing, spreadsheets) • Willingness to work flexible hours, including occasional evenings or weekends Physical Requirements • Ability to sit, stand, and move between locations within departmental facilities • Ability to lift and carry light to moderate materials or equipment, as needed Work Schedule • Hours vary based on departmental needs and student availability LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 12 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
