    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4723": {
      "title": "Student Worker-Tutor for Lewyt College Veterinary Medicine",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Student Worker-Tutor for Lewyt College Veterinary Medicine Student Worker-Tutor for Lewyt College Veterinary Medicine No. 4723 Long Island University Brookville, New York Learning Support Center (ARC) Posted Oct 05, 2026 $17 per hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 per hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Jun 30, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Name of the position: Student Worker/Tutor Is this a Federal Work Study position? Yes Campus: Post Description: Student Employee – POST CAMPUS TUTORS in THE LEARNING CENTER for College of Veterinarian courses Fall 2025 – Spring 2026. Tutors MUST be referred by Dr. Brendan Caputo and interviewed by Marie Fatscher BEFORE applying for the position. Department Name: The Learning Center Department’s Dean and/or Director: Marie Fatscher Location: Building and Floor: Library Main Floor Supervisor: Name: Marie Fatscher Title: Director of Learning Center Purpose or role of the position within the organization (Basic Function and Scope of Responsibilities): Tutoring for 1st year DVM courses: Veterinary Anatomy I, Physiology I, Histology, Immunology, Animal Welfare and Behavior, Anatomy II, Physiology II, Animal Nutrition, General Pathology. Tutoring for 2nd year DVM courses: Systemic Pathology I, Intro to Pharmacology, Veterinary Bacteriology & Mycology, Systemic Pathology II, Epidemiology, Pharmacology, Public Health and Food Safety. Duties and Principal Responsibilities: Work up to 12 hours per week in The Learning Center – located on the main floor of the Library. Education Requirements: LIU student enrolled in an active degree program, Must have 3.2 gpa and faculty or department chair recommendation for the courses you want to tutor Training, Skills, Knowledge, Experience: *All student candidates must complete an employment application and submit an updated resume.* Email: marie.fatscher@liu.edu Rate of Pay : minimum hourly rate $17 HR Period of employment: Begin Date: End Date: 5/2026 Evaluation procedures and schedules :  Flexible hours Monday – Friday 9:00 am to 6:00 pm; evenings and weekends via Zoom LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunities in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 13 Days Since Posted 4 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like Student Worker/Tutor for Humanities, Natural Scien... #4718 Learning Support Center (ARC) © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
