    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5036": {
      "title": "Women’s Rowing- Assistant Coach",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Women’s Rowing- Assistant Coach Women’s Rowing- Assistant Coach No. 5036 Long Island University Brookville, New York Athletics-Rowing Posted Sep 30, 2026 $40,000 - $45,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $40,000 - $45,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 30, 2026 Contact Complete online application Job Description Position Summary: Long Island University provides a wide array of athletic opportunities on both the \nintercollegiate and recreational levels which will enhance and enrich the educational \nexperience of our students, as well as provide recreational and fitness facilities and \nactivities for the entire University community. This full-time position is responsible for \nassisting the LIU Women’s Rowing Head Coach with recruiting, coaching, and counseling \nof student-athletes. Responsibilities: Assist with the fiscal responsibilities pertaining to preparing, monitoring, and \nverifying expenditures associated with program. Assist with leadership and instruction in the personal and athletic development of \nstudent athletes. Assist with planning, organization, and coaching of the rowing team. Support fundraising efforts for ongoing operation of rowing program. Evaluate and implement innovations in rowing strategy and equipment. Coach and instruct student-athletes in sport-specific skills, training techniques, \nand strategies through preparation, practice, and competition (race strategy), \nproviding guidance in both group and individual settings. Recruit student-athletes by identifying, evaluating, and vetting prospects, \ncoordinating communications and visits, and collaborating with admissions and \nfinancial aid to support enrollment. Collaborate with departmental staff to support operations, ensure compliance with \nNCAA, NEC, and University policies. Assist with the team’s travel planning, paperwork, budget management, and other \nadministrative duties. Candidate should be able to motivate recruits, athletes, and alumni to support the \nprogram enthusiastically. Other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree. A valid drivers license required. Strong communication, public relations, and management skills. Ability to work a flexible schedule including nights and weekends. Ability to work with a diverse campus constituency; including students, parents, \ncoaches, faculty, staff and alumni. Knowledge of NCAA policies and procedures preferred. 3 to 5 years of coaching experience required, preferably on the collegiate level. LIU Post campus is a scenic, historic, and\nscholarly campus that offers a small-school environment with the access and\nresources of a major metropolitan university. The University's 350+ acre campus\nis located on the estate of Marjorie Merriweather Post, 27 miles east of New\nYork City on Long Island's Gold Coast. The campus houses the Lewyt College of\nVeterinary Medicine, the first professional School of Accountancy, an\nAACSB-accredited Business School, and an award-winning theater program. LIU is\nhome to the world-renowned Tilles Center for the Performing Arts and the Shark\nStadium, where supporters gather to cheer on the Sharks’ Division I athletic\nprogram. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal \nopportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the \ndiversity and excellence of our academic community. We encourage applications \nfrom all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, religion, genetic information, \nsexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, \nnational origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, \ndisability, or any other basis protected by applicable laws. Hiring is contingent on \neligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 19 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like Head Coach - Women's Rowing... #4929 Athletics-Rowing © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
