    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/1751": {
      "title": "Federal Student Worker - Ceramic Studio Assistant",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Federal Student Worker - Ceramic Studio Assistant Federal Student Worker - Ceramic Studio Assistant No. 1751 Long Island University Brookville, New York Art Posted Sep 29, 2026 $17 an hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 an hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-exempt Application Deadline May 21, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Position Summary: The Ceramic Studio Assistant\nsupports the daily operation of the ceramics studio and helps maintain a clean,\norganized, and safe working environment for students, instructors, and studio\nmembers. Key Responsibilities: Prepare and organize\nclay, tools, glazes, and other studio materials. Maintain cleanliness of\n     worktables, sinks, floors, shelves, and shared equipment. Assist with loading and\n     unloading kilns under the direction of studio staff. Organize finished pieces, works\n     in progress, and student storage areas. Reclaim and recycle clay and\n     help manage studio waste. Mix or prepare glazes and other\n     ceramic materials as instructed. Assist instructors with class\n     setup and cleanup. Monitor studio supplies and\n     notify staff when materials need to be restocked. Help students and studio\n     members locate tools, materials, and equipment. Follow and help reinforce\n     studio safety procedures. Perform other general studio\n     maintenance and operational tasks as needed. Qualifications: Basic knowledge of\nceramics or willingness to learn. Reliable, organized, and\n     comfortable working independently. Able to perform physical studio\n     tasks, including lifting clay and supplies. Good communication skills and a\n     cooperative attitude. Previous ceramics, art studio,\n     or workshop experience is helpful but not required. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to\nextending 