      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Student Worker - Alumni & Employer Engagement Student Worker - Alumni & Employer Engagement No. 4450 Long Island University Brookville, New York Employer and Alumni Engagement Posted Sep 24, 2026 $17 per hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 per hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Mar 31, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Supervisor: Name: Brianna Kilker Title: Associate Director of Alumni & Employer Engagement Purpose or role of the position within the organization\n(Basic Function and Scope of Responsibilities): Engage with alumni, update their contact information, and encourage financial support for the university through the Annual Fund. The role involves informing alumni about upcoming events, achievements, and the impact of their contributions. Duties and Principal Responsibilities: The position involves reaching out to alumni to update their contact information, build rapport by discussing their experiences at LIU, and inform them about upcoming events and university achievements. The role includes encouraging alumni to support the Annual Fund by explaining its impact and securing financial contributions, while maintaining accurate records of interaction and donation status. Providing feedback on engagement strategies is essential to improve outreach efforts and alumni participation. Education Requirements: LIU student enrolled in an\nactive degree program Training, Skills, Knowledge, Experience: Rate of Pay : minimum hourly rate $17 HR Period of employment: Begin Date: 9/2026 End\nDate: 5/2027 Evaluation procedures and schedules : Evaluated on a continuous basis by supervisor. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to\nextending equal opportunities in employment to all qualified candidates who can\ncontribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU\nencourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race,\ncolor, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender\nidentity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity,\ncitizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other\nbasis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is\ncontingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 25 Days Since Posted 5 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
