    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5033": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach - Men’s and Women’s Tennis",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Assistant Coach - Men’s and Women’s Tennis Assistant Coach - Men’s and Women’s Tennis No. 5033 Long Island University Brookville, New York Athletics-Tennis Posted Sep 24, 2026 $32,000- $37,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $32,000- $37,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 24, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Position Summary: Long Island University (LIU) seeks a dedicated and enthusiastic Assistant Men’s and \nWomen’s Tennis Coach to support the head coach in all aspects of the men’s and women’s \ntennis programs. This full-time assistant coach position involves assisting with practice \nplanning, player development, recruitment, and program administration, contributing to a \ncompetitive and positive team environment. Responsibilities: Coaching and Leadership : Collaborate with the head coach to develop and \nexecute comprehensive coaching plans focused on enhancing tennis skills, \nperformance, and team dynamics. Foster a culture of excellence, accountability, \nand sportsmanship. Recruitment : Actively identify and recruit top-tier student-athletes who align with \nLIU’s academic and athletic standards. Build and maintain relationships with high \nschool coaches, club programs, and recruitment networks. Team Management : Oversee all aspects of team operations, including organizing \npractice schedules, preparing for competition, developing strategies, and ensuring \noptimal performance and safety of student-athletes. Academic Support : Work closely with academic advisors to monitor the academic \nprogress of student-athletes, ensuring they meet the university’s academic \nexpectations. Compliance : Maintain a high level of integrity by ensuring the program adheres to \nNCAA, conference, and university rules and regulations. Community Engagement : Represent the program positively within the campus and \nlocal communities. Foster relationships with alumni, fans, and donors to increase \nprogram visibility and support. Budget Management : Assist with managing the program’s budget, ensuring fiscal \nresponsibility and resource optimization. Qualifications: Experience: Minimum of 2 years of coaching experience at the NCAA level (or \nsimilar high-level experience). A proven track record in developing and recruiting \nstudent-athletes. Skills: Strong leadership, communication, and organizational skills. Ability to \ninspire and motivate student-athletes both on and off the court. Knowledge: In-depth knowledge of NCAA rules, regulations, and policies. Personal Attributes: Passion for student-athlete development both academically \nand athletically. Strong work ethic, integrity, and commitment to excellence. Ability \nto work collaboratively with colleagues, staff, and administration. Preferred Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree. Previous coaching experience at an NCAA Division I program. Proven success in recruitment and talent development. Experience in building community outreach and increasing program visibility. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in \nemployment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence \nof our academic community. We encourage applications from all qualified individuals \nregardless of race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or \nexpression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran \nor military status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable laws. Hiring is \ncontingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 25 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
