    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5032": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach - Softball",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Assistant Coach - Softball Assistant Coach - Softball No. 5032 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Athletics-Women's Softball Posted Sep 24, 2026 $35,000 - $40,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $35,000 - $40,000 Start Date AS soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 24, 2026 Contact Please submit online application Job Description Position Summary: Long Island University (LIU) is seeking a highly motivated and knowledgeable individual to \njoin its NCAA Division I Women’s Softball program as Assistant Coach. This full-time position, based on \nthe LIU Brooklyn campus for the 2026-27 academic year and the LIU Post Campus beginning with the \n2027-28 academic year, will work closely with the LIU Softball Head Coach to support all aspects of \nthe program. The LIU Softball Assistant Coach position responsibilities will include a broad range of \ncoaching and operational duties that contribute to the overall success of the team. \nThe ideal candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to fostering a competitive and positive \nteam culture, supporting student-athletes in their academic and athletic growth, and upholding the \nvalues and standards of LIU Athletics. Key Responsibilities: Assist the Head Coach in developing, planning, and implementing practice sessions and game \nstrategies. Mentor and support student-athletes in both athletic and personal development. Recruit prospective student-athletes through on-campus visits, travel, and regular communication, in \ncompliance with NCAA and NEC regulations. Coordinate video breakdown and analysis for scouting, game preparation, and player feedback. Monitor academic progress of student-athletes in collaboration with academic advisors. Maintain a thorough knowledge of NCAA, NEC, and LIU policies to ensure full program compliance. Assist with team travel logistics, budgeting, equipment management, and other administrative \nduties. Represent LIU at conferences, meetings, and community events as assigned. Help foster a positive, inclusive, and accountable team environment. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred. Minimum of 1–3 years of coaching experience at the collegiate level, preferably NCAA Division I. Strong knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations. Demonstrated success in recruiting and player development. Excellent organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and travel as required. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunities in \nemployment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our \nacademic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to \nrace, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or \nexpression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military \nstatus, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is \ncontingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 25 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4142": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor of Media Arts and Film",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Adjunct Professor of Media Arts and Film Adjunct Professor of Media Arts and Film No. 4142 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Media Arts Posted Sep 23, 2026 $1,100 - $1,450 per credit Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Adjunct Faculty Salary Range $1,100 - $1,450 per credit Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Feb 26, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description The Polk School at Long Island University Brooklyn is seeking to hire an\nAssistant Professor of Media Arts and Film beginning January 2027. The position offers a\nteaching load of up to 9 credits. Additional responsibilities include student advising and\nrecruiting as well as participation in faculty committees. The candidate must hold an MFA and\nhave experience teaching and working in one of the following areas: film producing, digital film\nproduction, cinematography, producing, and/or production management. Our ideal candidate is\ncapable of teaching undergraduate courses about Media production and film theory. The Polk School is composed of faculty with extensive experience in the film\nindustry doing directing, cinematography, producing, and editing. It includes four programs:\nMedia Arts, Film & TV, Acting for Film and TV, and Writing and Producing for Television. LIU Brooklyn offers over 125 academic programs serving approximately 6,000 students. It is\none of the fastest growing and most ethnically diverse campuses in the metropolitan area\nlocated in the heart of downtown Brooklyn, just one subway stop away from Manhattan. Applicants must apply via the online application portal (https://jobs.liu.edu/#/list/F) by submitting\na cover letter, curriculum vitae, and three references with names and contact information.\nReview of applications will begin immediately. The application window is open until the position\nis filled. LIU conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent\noffer. Adjunct Instructor: $1,100 Adjunct Assistant: $1,200 Adjunct Associate: $1,350 Adjunct Full: $1,450 LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in\nemployment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our\nacademic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard\nto race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or\nexpression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or\nmilitary status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal\nlaws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 25 Days Since Posted 3 Positions Available Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
