    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4643": {
      "title": "Instructor Au Pair",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Instructor Au Pair Instructor Au Pair No. 4643 Long Island University Brookville, New York Au Pair Posted Sep 21, 2026 $1,000-$1,200 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Staff Salary Range $1,000-$1,200 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 31, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Instructor, University Au Pair Certificate Program (Part-Time) Position Overview: As part of their J-1 visa requirements, au pairs in the US must complete the equivalent of 6\ncollege credits (a total of 72 hours) from an accredited university during a 12 month period.\nLIU’s University Au Pair Certificate Program has educated thousands of au pairs in a wide\nvariety of topics, including childhood development, English language skills, American history\nand government, fashion, merchandising, international diplomacy, arts and culture, sports,\nsocial media marketing, business and many other exciting topics. A combination of live\nclassroom discussion, interaction with other au pairs, caring university instructors and engaging\nactivities provide a holistic approach to immersion into the unique culture of the United States. The successful candidate for the position of Instructor of the University Au Pair Certificate\nProgram will provide learning experiences for au pairs that will deepen and extend their\nintellectual interests as well as develop the skills of independent learning. Instructors should be\nknowledgeable and supportive of visiting international students to the USA and design creative\nlearning experiences to accommodate the diversity of learning styles and English levels in an\nadult population, ages 18-26. Classes are held in person on LIU Post’s campus in Brookville,\nLong Island, New York a minimum of one weekend per month. In person and online classes run\nFri, 5pm-9m, Sat 9am-6pm and Sun 9am-1pm. Pre coursework and post coursework are to be\ngiven in addition to the in-person classes to equal 36 hours of instruction. Reports to: Director of Au Pair Certificate Program Qualifications and Skills: • Master’s Degree Preferred • NYS Permanent Teaching Certification (K-12) in Teacher Education a plus • Minimum of 5 year teaching experience preferred • Excellent reading, writing and communication skills • Knowledge of facilitating curriculum that is project and inquiry based,\nemphasizing critical thinking with interdisciplinary connections • Must be able to teach using different types of media • Evidence of originality, initiative, commitment to excellence, and enthusiasm for\nteaching • Flexible teaching style SALARY: Commensurate with experience, part-time, no benefits, non-union, non-tenured track\nposition. Position is subject to a background check. Vaccination preferred. INFORMATION: post-aupair@liu.edu | 516-299-4193 LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 27 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Staff Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5027": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Student Success and Student-Run Businesses",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Associate Director of Student Success and Student-Run Businesses Associate Director of Student Success and Student-Run Businesses No. 5027 Long Island University Brookville, New York Student Affairs-Post Posted Sep 21, 2026 $65,000 - $70,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $65,000 - $70,000 Start Date As Soon As Possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 21, 2026 Contact Please complete online application Job Description Position Summary The Associate Director of Student Success\nand Student-Run Businesses supports student success while contributing to the\nstrategy and operations of LIU’s student-run businesses, including the Canteen\nStore, Student Fashion Store, and Shark Nation Spirit Store. The position\nmanages a designated student caseload, providing individualized coaching and\nsupport, while working closely with colleagues to advance business performance,\nstudent employment, experiential learning, and professional development. Key Responsibilities Student-Run Businesses Contribute to the strategy, growth, and development of the student\n     run businesses. Partner with the Store Manager on business goals, operations,\n     merchandising, customer engagement, and special initiatives. Help create meaningful experiential learning, leadership, and\n     career development opportunities through the student-run businesses. Support recruitment, onboarding, training, coaching, and\n     development of Federal Work Study students and Sales Ambassadors. Assist with retail operations, inventory, e-commerce, Shopify\n     POS, promotions, events, and customer service. Use business and student feedback to identify opportunities for\n     improvement and growth. Student Success & Coaching Manage a designated caseload of students and provide\n     individualized coaching, advising, and proactive outreach. Help students address academic, personal, and professional\n     challenges and connect them with appropriate campus resources. Develop success plans and monitor student progress toward\n     academic and professional goals. Provide coaching related to goal setting, time management,\n     career readiness, leadership, and self-advocacy. Collaborate with campus partners to support student engagement,\n     persistence, retention, and overall success. Help students identify and articulate transferable skills\n     gained through employment, leadership, and experiential learning. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and\n     relevant experience. Experience working directly with college students through\n     advising, coaching, student success, career development, or related work. Experience in retail, business operations, customer service, or\n     a related field. Experience supervising, coaching, or developing student\n     employees or staff. Retail management experience preferred. Experience with Shopify POS or comparable systems preferred. Physical & Work Environment\nRequirements Ability to lift, carry, push, and pull up to 50 pounds. Ability to stand and walk for extended periods and perform\n     frequent bending, reaching, and lifting. Must be able to work occasional evenings, weekends, campus\n     events, and other Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 27 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like Success Coach and Residence Life Coordinator... #5011 Student Affairs-Post © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4413": {
      "title": "Adjunct Associate Professor - Natural & Life Sciences",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Adjunct Associate Professor - Natural & Life Sciences Adjunct Associate Professor - Natural & Life Sciences No. 4413 Long Island University Brookville, New York Biology, Earth and Environmentl Science Posted Sep 21, 2026 $1,000-$1,350 per credit Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Adjunct Faculty Salary Range $1,000-$1,350 per credit Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Aug 31, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description College of Science-Post\nPart-Time Faculty Available in Natural and Life Sciences Position Description: The Department of Natural and Life Sciences at Long Island University (LIU) Post is\ninviting applications for part-time faculty in Biology, Chemistry, Biochemistry, Earth Science,\nMathematics, Physics and all other related areas in Natural and Life Sciences. The candidates\nneed to adapt to a fast-paced learning environment and be proactive, creative, self-motivated\nand have a strong desire to introduce project-based and experiential learning opportunities in\nthe assigned courses and labs. Professional experience and/or equivalent research experiences\nare highly desired. Required Minimum Qualifications: - M.S. degree or Ph.D. in the areas of teaching interest - Ability to teach various undergraduate courses and labs - Excellent communication skills - Commitment for project-based learning and excellence and effectiveness in teaching Application Procedures: A full application must include a cover letter describing the applicant’s teaching interest,\na CV, teaching evaluations if applicable, and a list of two references, including names, email,\naddress, and telephone number. Only electronic documents will be accepted. Please complete the on-line application in\naddition to providing the required documents. All required documents must be submitted for\nreview consideration. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in\nemployment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our\nacademic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard\nto race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or\nexpression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or\nmilitary status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal\nlaws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 28 Days Since Posted 12 Positions Available Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
