    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5025": {
      "title": "Legal Assistant/Paralegal",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Legal Assistant/Paralegal Legal Assistant/Paralegal No. 5025 Long Island University University Center - Brookville, New York Counsel Posted Sep 17, 2026 $71,500 - $75,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Staff Salary Range $71,500 - $75,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-exempt Application Deadline May 01, 2027 Contact HR@liu.edu Job Description Office of the General Counsel Basic Function and Scope of\nResponsibilities The Legal Assistant supports the\nOffice of the General Counsel with contract processing, litigation support, and\ndaily administrative operations. Principal Responsibilities Contract Processing Serves as the intake point for all contracts\n     submitted to the legal department. Reviews contracts for completeness, tracks the agreement\n     through approval and execution, and follows up with departments and\n     counterparties to keep matters moving. Maintains the contract tracking system and updates\n     the status of contracts, affiliation agreements, and other agreements in\n     real time. Serves as the first point of contact to discuss\n     contracts approval process and responds to questions from administrative\n     departments. Litigation and Compliance\nSupport Tracks and manages the case docket, including court\n     deadlines, arbitration hearings, agency filings, and cases assigned to\n     outside counsel. Drafts responses to subpoenas and coordinates the\n     collection and production of responsive records. Handles FERPA requests and other educational and\n     employment record requests in coordination with the appropriate University\n     offices. Communicates with insurance carriers regarding\n     claims, coverage questions, and litigation updates. Prepares general correspondence, pleadings, response\n     papers, and other legal documents under attorney supervision. Financial Administration Processes and tracks outside counsel invoices and\n     legal fees, confirms compliance with billing guidelines, and coordinates\n     payment. Office Administration Answers and directs calls, responds to inquiries, and\n     opens and routes incoming mail. Maintains the legal department filing system, both\n     physical and electronic. Manages calendars, schedules meetings, and\n     coordinates arbitration hearings and court appearances. Works regularly with departments across the\n     University, outside counsel, insurance carriers, and vendors. Performs other related duties as assigned. Education Requirements Associate degree and at least\ntwo years of office experience. Experience in a legal environment is preferred.\nParalegal certification is a plus. Training, Skills, Knowledge,\nand Experience Works effectively in an extremely busy environment\n     and manages competing priorities with strong attention to detail. Handles confidential and sensitive information with\n     discretion. Works well as part of a team and takes initiative\n     when working independently. Working Conditions: Office environment Materials and Equipment: Computer, telephone, copier, and scanner LIU is an equal opportunity\nemployer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all\nqualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our\nacademic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals\nwithout regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual\norientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental\nstatus, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military\nstatus, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable local, Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 32 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Staff Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
