      "title": "Secretary Level 6 - Local 153",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Secretary Level 6 - Local 153 Secretary Level 6 - Local 153 No. 5003 Long Island University Brookville, New York Dean-Arts and Design, LIU Post Posted Sep 15, 2026 48,296 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Staff Salary Range 48,296 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Nov 30, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary Assists with the day-to-day running of the Dean’s Office. Responsibilities Serves as initial face-to-face and telephone contact point for students, faculty members and outside visitors. Each semester collects Outside Additional Professional Activities forms, syllabi, and any other required documents or materials Assist students/faculty/staff in obtaining documentation in connection with student registrations, change of grades, VISA forms, permission codes, etc. Prepares and processes required electronic filing of workloads Process invoices, reimbursements, and required documentation for payment Make appointments and schedules meetings as requested Responsible for the ordering of office supplies and maintaining inventory Responsible for internal and external mail Maintains college’s lists including, telephone list, room list, adjunct faculty list, etc. Other duties as assigned by the College leadership Requirements Candidate must possess a professional demeanor, excellent communication and customer service skills, interpersonal, organizational and computer skills.  Working knowledge of Microsoft Word, Microsoft Teams, Excel, Outlook, Power Point, other Microsoft Suite products, Sharepoint, Peoplesoft and experience working in a professional environment. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable local, state, or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 34 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Staff Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
