    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5022": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – Master of Public Health (MPH) Program",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Adjunct Faculty – Master of Public Health (MPH) Program Adjunct Faculty – Master of Public Health (MPH) Program No. 5022 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Master of Public HealthProgram Posted Sep 08, 2026 $1,000 - $1,350 per credit Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Adjunct Faculty Salary Range $1,000 - $1,350 per credit Start Date As soon as Possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 08, 2026 Contact Complete Online application Job Description Position Summary: The Master of Public Health (MPH) Program at Long Island University seeks a qualified Adjunct Faculty member to teach MPH 740: Program Planning and Evaluation during the Fall 2026 semester.\nThe successful candidate will possess expertise in public health program planning, implementation, and evaluation, with the ability to teach graduate students using current evidence-based practices and applied public health frameworks. The instructor will be responsible for developing and delivering engaging course content; preparing a syllabus that outlines course objectives, learning outcomes, instructional methods, assignments, and grading policies; maintaining the course in Brightspace; conducting weekly class sessions either in person or synchronously via Microsoft Teams in accordance with the program schedule; maintaining regular office hours to provide academic support and mentoring to students; and fulfilling all University responsibilities related to grading, attendance, and academic policies.\nFaculty are expected to create an engaging and inclusive learning environment that promotes critical thinking, evidence-based decision making, ethical reasoning, effective communication, and the application of public health principles to contemporary health challenge. Required Qualifications: Doctoral degree (Ph.D. or DrPH) in Public Health or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated expertise in public health program planning, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation. Evidence of successful graduate-level teaching or training experience. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching and student learning. Evidence of continued professional growth and scholarly or professional engagement in public health. Relevant public health practice experience in government, healthcare, nonprofit organizations, academia, or related settings. Excellent communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to integrate theory, evidence, policy, and professional practice into graduate instruction. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching in a face-to-face environment. Experience with Brightspace or comparable learning management systems. Professional experience working with public health agencies, healthcare systems,\ncommunity organizations, or governmental organizations. Experience with accreditation standards, competency-based education, and applied public\nhealth practice. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive, equitable, and student-centered teaching\npractices. Responsibilities: Teach MPH 740: Program Planning and Evaluation in accordance with the approved\ncourse description and MPH Program competency-based student learning outcomes. Prepare and submit a course syllabus that aligns with program requirements, University\npolicies, and accreditation standards. Develop lectures, learning activities, assignments, and assessments that promote critical\nthinking and application of program planning and evaluation concepts. Maintain an organized and up-to-date Brightspace course site. Meet all scheduled classes and adhere to the University's academic calendar, including\nfinal examination and grading deadlines. Maintain regular communication with students and provide weekly office hours. Submit attendance, grades, and other required reports according to University deadlines. Participate in program meetings, assessment activities, accreditation initiatives, and\ncurriculum discussions when requested. Adhere to University policies and maintain the highest standards of professionalism,\nacademic integrity, and ethical conduct. Equal Opportunity Employer\nLong Island University is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal\nemployment opportunities to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and\nexcellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified\nindividuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation,\ngender, gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity,\ncitizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other status protected by\napplicable federal, state, or local law.\nEmployment is contingent upon eligibility to work in the United State Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 41 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
