    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5019": {
      "title": "Education Specialist",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Education Specialist Education Specialist No. 5019 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Community Grants & Partnership Posted Sep 04, 2026 $45 an hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $45 an hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Dec 04, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary The Education Specialist will coordinate academic instruction for the Advantage After-School Program and Advantage Summer Program at MS 113 The Ronald Edmonds Learning Center. Programming occurs at MS 113 The Ronald Edmonds Learning Center.   Flexible work schedule. Key Responsibilities Integrate day school learning into Advantage programming. Collaborate with teachers, instructors, and group leaders to support student academic and social development. Observe classroom instructions. Facilitate academic instruction for Scholars Lab (mathematics, English, etc.). Assist in student recruitment. Inform parents/guardians about student progress. Prepare required reports, surveys, and attendance forms; maintain appropriate records. Perform other duties as assigned by the Program Director. Minimum Qualifications Master’s Degree in Education, Psychology or Social Work.  License in Education or Social Work required.  Applicants must be proficient in MS Window XP, Word, Excel, Vista, and Power Point.  Five (5) years of teaching and/or administrative experience.   Experience in out-of-school programming. LIU is an equal opportunity employer.  LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital s