    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5016": {
      "title": "Success Coach - Financial Aid",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Success Coach - Financial Aid Success Coach - Financial Aid No. 5016 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Center for Student Success and Coaching-Brooklyn Posted Sep 04, 2026 66,300 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range 66,300 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 04, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary The Success Coach will be a student's primary point of contact for everything at the University—from academic advisement and campus involvement to financial aid counseling and career development. The coach will help students chart and navigate an individual path within the LIU community. Working one-on-one with students, the Success Coach will create a success plan tailored to each student's needs, goals, and interests. This plan will assist students in choosing courses, selecting a major, finding scholarships, internships, and study abroad opportunities, and launching their careers. Success Coaches will keep students on track toward graduation and help ensure a seamless transition from college student to successful professional. Reporting to an Associate Director, the Success Coach may specialize in and execute functions in the following areas: First & Second Year Student Success, Third & Fourth Year Student Success, Graduate & International Student Success, Residence Life, and Campus Life. Ancillary duties will include financial aid packaging, awarding/posting of aid, and other related tasks. Key Responsibilities Serve as the primary advisor for a caseload of students, providing individualized guidance and support. Facilitate students’ transition to the university, ensuring students are integrated into the intellectual, cultural, and social life of the institution. Assist with pre-enrollment activities, admissions, orientation, campus events, and career initiatives, reinforcing the importance of a holistic, integrated college experience aimed at academic and career success. Provide academic advisement, guiding students from initial registration through major/degree selection, aligning their academic choices with career interests and goals. Assist students with registration inquiries and processes, including add/drop procedures, graduation information, and general student application questions. Offer career counseling and resources to help students develop a career path aligned with their academic pursuits. Participate in presenting financial aid workshops, orientation activities, open houses, and other departmental and student events as needed. Deliver excellent customer service by supporting the regular coverage of the department phone queue, answering questions related to financial aid and enrollment processes for students and their families. Assist in evaluating transfer credits for courses taken at postsecondary institutions, considering the educational quality of the learning experience. Support financial aid functions in alignment with the guidelines set by the New York State Financial Aid Administrators Association (NYSFAAA). Collaborate with counterparts on other campuses to ensure consistent operations and a uniform student experience across the LIU system. Perform other duties as assigned by the Associate Directors/Directors of Financial Aid Ancillary Duties Maintain knowledge of federal and state financial regulations, as well as university financial policies and procedures. Assist students in understanding financial aid processes and help outline a plan for financing their education, including personal finances, student loans, government grants, and private scholarships. Support the collection and processing of required documents for all students. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s preferred At least 1-3 years of progressively responsible professional experience in higher education, enrollment services, student affairs, or academic affairs; sound judgment and decision-making skills. • Excellent oral and written communication skills. High energy and enthusiasm for working with students and helping them achieve success. Ability to design and implement innovative programs with strong attention to detail. Strong interpersonal communication skills. Proficiency in computer skills/literacy. Occasional travel to/from other LIU campuses for the facilitation of training sessions, meetings, and other university functions. Excellent oral and written communication skills. High energy and enthusiasm to work with students and propel them toward success. Ability to design and implement innovative programs with a strong attention to detail. Interpersonal communication skills Computer skills/literacy LIU is an equal opportunity employer.  LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military statue, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 45 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like Director, Center for Student Success & Coaching... #4965 Center for Student Success and Coaching-Brooklyn Success Coach... #4278 Center for Student Success and Coaching-Brooklyn © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/1867": {
      "title": "FWS Student Worker - Event Attendee",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU FWS Student Worker - Event Attendee FWS Student Worker - Event Attendee No. 1867 Long Island University Brookville, New York Tilles Audience Services Posted Sep 03, 2026 $17 per hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 per hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Jul 01, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Front of House\nHours:  Varies depending on show, primarily evenings and\nweekends.  Very flexible schedule Event Attendees main\nresponsibility is assisting the managers with crowd control and for assisting\nthe bartenders during the performance. Event Attendees also have the ability to\nwork as a Box Office Associate. Event Attendees are also responsible for\nthe following: Making sure the concession\n     stand and kitchen are clean and ready before and after a performance. Selling of concessions or\n     merchandise during a performance Helping the managers with crowd\n     controls for VIP events, Meet & Greet, etc. Helping the managers with main\n     set up for each performance.  *This may require lite heavy\n     lifting* During emergency situations,\n     helping the house manager guide all patrons out of the theater calmly and\n     orderly. Desired skills and\ntraits: Able to work well under\n     pressure, in a fast paced environment Customer service experience Cash- handling\n     experience.  (Preferred but not required) Excellent communication skills Positive, can do attitude Team player Box Office Qualifications and Responsibilities: Ticketing and assisting\nguest via phone or in-person, by email or in-person Troubleshoot e-ticket\naccess for customers Proficiency in\nMicrosoft suite Prior ticketing\nsoftware/POS experience a plus but not required Strong communication\nand organizational skills LIU\nis an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal\nopportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the\ndiversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all\nqualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information,\nsexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or\nparental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or\nmilitary status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable\nlocal, state or federal laws. Hiring is\ncontingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 45 Days Since Posted 17 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like FWS- Box Office Representative ... #5039 Tilles Audience Services © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
