    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5009": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions No. 5009 Long Island University Brookville, New York Admissions (Post) Posted Sep 03, 2026 $62,000 - $66,300 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $62,000 - $66,300 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 03, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary This position has a primary focus on domestic, first year undergraduate student recruitment and admissions counseling. There will also be some cross-recruitment with other markets, including but not limited to International, Transfer and Graduate Admissions. It incorporates a full range of admissions responsibilities including establishing and strengthening a recruitment territory, representing the University to school counselors, prospective students and family members, evaluating admissions applications, and contributing to the planning and implementation of admissions projects and activities. The position is located on the Post campus but the Assistant Director will represent the Post, Brooklyn and Global campuses of LIU. The Assistant Director is responsible for practicing good student service principles and embracing a holistic student development strategic plan. This position requires an understanding of best practices in higher education and admissions. Admissions staff will act as advocates, advisers, and counselors. The Assistant Director is required to understand educational systems including but not limited to secondary schools (U.S. based and international); community colleges; associate and baccalaureate degrees; and post-bac/post doc programs. The Assistant Director is responsible for having a sensitivity to adolescent and college-student development. Key Responsibilities Responsible for meeting enrollment goals. Counsel prospective students in the office, via telephone, Zoom, and e-mail regarding LIU academic programs, admissions policies and procedures, and other enrollment-related information. Represent LIU at high school college fairs, high school college visits, instant decision days, open houses, and other recruitment events; extended/frequent overnight travel is required. Prepare and deliver presentations to small and large groups; conduct student interviews; provide information and guidance to prospective students and their families. Establish and develop contacts with high schools, colleges, and recruitment partners. Provide outreach to individuals and organizations; supply organizations with information pertaining to LIU for distribution to prospective students. Assist with the planning and execution of on- and off-campus yield events and open houses. Review applications and render admissions and scholarship decisions for applicants. Provide regular outreach to applicants and prospective students (from inquiry through enrollment stages). Serve as a liaison to Academic Deans and other campus partners on matters related to current initiatives, as well as new programs, recruitment, and the establishment of new markets. Prepare reports for the Director of Campus Admissions to monitor the status of applicants, activities, and projects. Develop a recruitment strategy and schedule for assigned territories by deciding which schools to target for recruitment; formulating recruitment goals; evaluating and recommending whether to consider targeting schools in the future; and tracking progress. Recommend strategies to enhance the University’s marketing efforts, including implementing new outreach efforts to guidance counselors and others, as well as creating and sending individual communications to students and others. Foster relationships with high school Guidance Counselors; participate in regional and national counseling associations; make presentations to schools and communities on behalf of the University. Other duties, as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree required, Master’s degree preferred. Experience in Admissions or a related field is highly desired. The Assistant Director must be proficient in all Microsoft Office applications, including but not limited to Word, Excel, Outlook, and Power Point. Previous experience using PeopleSoft and Image Now systems is preferred. The Assistant Director must possess excellent written and oral communications skills. Additionally, the Assistant Director must exhibit strong interpersonal and time management skills. Positive attitude and ability to work in a team environment is necessary. Working Conditions This position operates in an office setting, Monday through Friday; however, frequent evening and weekend hours are required. Travel within New York and out-of-state is required. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 46 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like Associate Director of Graduate Admissions and Recr... #5012 Admissions (Post) Associate Director of National Recruitment... #4677 Admissions (Post) © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5014": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Campus Life",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Associate Director of Campus Life Associate Director of Campus Life No. 5014 Long Island University Brookville, New York Center for Student Success and Coaching-Brookville Posted Sep 03, 2026 $66,300 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $66,300 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 03, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary The Associate Director of Campus Life provides operational leadership for the University’s student engagement initiatives. This position oversees the daily administration of student clubs and organizations, fraternity and sorority life, community service programming, and large-scale student-focused programming. Working collaboratively with campus partners, the Associate Director ensures students engage in meaningful engagement opportunities that contribute to students’ sense of belonging and retention to the University. The Associate Director also serves as a Success Coach for a caseload of students.  Acting as a student’s primary point of contact, the Success Coach provides personalized guidance in academic planning, financial aid navigation, campus engagement, and career readiness. Coaches work one-on-one with students to develop tailored success plans aligned with their goals, interests, and strengths while supporting course selection, major exploration, scholarship access, internship guidance, study abroad opportunities, and post-graduation planning. Key Responsibilities Supervision & Department Operations Supervise professional staff and student employees responsible for various areas of campus life. Assist with recruitment, hiring, training, scheduling, supervision, and evaluation of orientation staff and office student workers Develop and maintain, in collaboration with Student Affairs leadership, departmental procedures that improve operational efficiency, customer service, and consistency across campus life areas. Assist with budget oversight, purchasing, inventory management, and operational planning for the department. Collaboration & Student Support Serve as a primary liaison with campus partners regarding campus life programming. Assist students and families in resolving concerns while providing exceptional customer service throughout the student life experience. Assessment & Compliance Monitor operational metrics to evaluate departmental effectiveness and identify opportunities for improvement. Ensure compliance with University policies, FERPA, Clery Act requirements, ADA/Section 504, and other applicable federal, state, and institutional guidelines, in conjunction with campus partners. Prepare reports related to campus life operational performance for divisional leadership. University Engagement Support major University initiatives, including Orientation, Open Houses, Admitted Student Days, Welcome Week, Homecoming and Family Weekend, Commencement, and other enrollment and student engagement activities. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of the Center for Student Success and Coaching and the Student Affairs leadership team. Success Coach Responsibilities Serve as the primary advisor and success coach for an assigned caseload of students, providing individualized support for academic, personal, and professional development. Guide students through the LIU Four-Year Model, from pre-enrollment and orientation through graduation, helping them integrate into the academic, social, and cultural life of the University. Support students with course registration, major selection, and degree planning aligned with their long-term career goals. Interpret career assessment tools and coach students in developing career paths that complement their academic pursuits. Assist students in navigating financial aid processes, including reviewing award information and understanding deadlines, procedures, and funding options. Plan and implement student success programming, including life planning seminars, academic workshops, and campus engagement initiatives that foster belonging and holistic development. Provide leadership in a designated area of academic success, campus life, residence life, and financial success. Collaborate with key departments across campus including but not limited to Admissions, Academic Affairs, Alumni and Employer Engagement, The Honors College, Learning Support Services, Athletics, to support recruitment, engagement, and retention strategies. Monitor student progress and maintain accurate records, submitting regular reports on retention, registration, and coaching outcomes. Support pre-enrollment and transition activities such as admissions events, orientation, and four-year programming. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of the Center for Student Success & Coaching. Minimum Requirements Bachelor’s degree required. Master's degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Educational Leadership, Business Administration, or a related field preferred. 3-5 years of progressively responsible experience in Student Life or Student Affairs. Experience managing student organizations, fraternity and sorority life, and/or campus programming. Demonstrated experience administering student life policies and procedures. Experience supervising professional and/or student staff. Strong organizational, project management, customer service, and problem-solving skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining exceptional attention to detail. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite. Working Conditions Flexible hours, including weekends and evenings, are required to execute this position including office and university events. Occasional travel to/from other LIU campuses for the facilitation of trainings, meetings and other university functions Materials & Equipment Computer, Microsoft Suite, PeopleSoft, Texting Platform, copier, phone LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, marital or veteran status, or Vietnam-era veteran status, or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 46 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like Success Coach and Greek Life Coordinator... #5013 Center for Student Success and Coaching-Brookville © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5012": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Graduate Admissions and Recruitment",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Associate Director of Graduate Admissions and Recruitment Associate Director of Graduate Admissions and Recruitment No. 5012 Long Island University Brookville, New York Admissions (Post) Posted Sep 03, 2026 $66,300 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $66,300 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 03, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary The Associate Director is responsible for supporting the overall recruitment strategies and matriculation of all new graduate students. The Associate Director will maintain adequate knowledge of admissions practices, admissions policies, academic programs and campus services. The Associate Director will ensure that all information supplied to prospective candidates and their families (when applicable) will be tendered in a sensitive and timely manner. Travel to recruitment events off-campus is required. Responsibilities will also include on-campus events and organizing candidate interviews. Throughout the recruitment process, the Associate Director will interact with prospective candidates through the stages of inquiry, application, decision, deposit, and matriculation, as well as, other units of the LIU Admissions Office.  The Associate Director reports directly to the Director of Graduate Admissions and the Assistant Vice President of Admissions. Key Responsibilities Develop and implement new recruitment strategies/initiatives and partnerships with feeder schools. Maintain and strengthen existing relationships with feeder schools. Review candidate transcripts and application materials to prepare admissions files for review. Create, review and update recruitment tools as necessary. Organize and host events (in-person or virtual) for prospective students. Establish and maintain recruitment schedules and events for local and national markets. Serve as an admissions liaison to various high schools and recruitment organizations. Timely communication with all prospective inquiries and applicants. Organize and host admissions interviews. Provide guidance to all candidates through the stages of decision, deposit, matriculation, and ensure all admissions requirements have been satisfied. Other duties as assigned by the Director of Graduate Admissions and the Assistant Vice President of Admissions. Minimum Requirements Bachelor’s Degree required; Master’s Degree preferred 3-5 years’ experience in college admissions, recruitment or marketing; student development and/or counseling experience; familiarity with and understanding of educational systems Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Strong customer service skills and experience; understanding of the dynamic modes of communication with students and parents (i.e.; use of technology and social networking vs. traditional use of email, phone campaigns and letter campaigns) Knowledge of CAS (centralized application service), CRM, Image Now and People Soft preferred. Ability to handle multiple assignments and responsibilities at the same time. Ability to adapt to a fast-paced work environment and work with diverse populations. Represent LIU at fairs, open houses, and other recruitment events; overnight travel is required. Familiarity with major metropolitan U.S. markets. Creativity, team-oriented work ethic; ability to work autonomously and with direction; flexibility for work schedules that may include evenings and weekends LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 46 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions ... #5009 Admissions (Post) Associate Director of National Recruitment... #4677 Admissions (Post) © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5015": {
      "title": "Licensed Veterinary Technician - Large Animal Ambulatory Rotation",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Licensed Veterinary Technician - Large Animal Ambulatory Rotation Licensed Veterinary Technician - Large Animal Ambulatory Rotation No. 5015 Long Island University Brookville, New York Veterinary Clinical Sciences Posted Sep 03, 2026 $66,300-$70,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $66,300-$70,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 03, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary Long Island University’s Lewyt College of Veterinary Medicine seeks a full-time Licensed Veterinary Technician for their Large Animal Ambulatory Services. This position supports the Service’s on-going clinical rotations for Year 4/final year veterinary students traveling with the College’s large animal clinicians to equine and livestock owners and facilities on Long Island and in the greater Tri-State area. Key Responsibilities Actively maintain inventory of equipment and consumables Maintain critical inventory logs Detailed cleansing & maintenance of surgical, radiography & ultrasonography equipment Maintain equipment service logs Maintain and Monitor Electronic Medical Records Systems Assist in Ambulatory Vehicle Driving Clean and Stock Ambulatory Vehicles Assist with Student and Clinician Communication Assist with Client Communication and Scheduling Assist in Training of Students Tabulate Student Case Activities Within the Ambulatory Rotations Perform the Service’s In-House Laboratory Work Cleansing, Packing, and Autoclave Sterilization of Surgical Instruments Laundering of Surgical Drapes, Wraps, and Work Wear Aid in Similar Support of the Complementary Equine Ambulatory Rotation Other Duties as Assigned Minimum Qualifications Licensed Veterinary Technician required Diligent Work Ethic When Independent of Constant Personal Supervision Excellent Time Management Strong Organizational Skills Attention to Detail Accurate, Precise, and Complete Documentation Skills Clear, Concise Written and Verbal Communication Skills Skilled in MS Outlook, Excel and Word 2 Years of Food Animal Husbandry Experience; Other Large Animal, Such as Equine, Experience Is Desired Skill and Experience in Large Animal Restraint and Handling Driver’s License, Safe Driving Record Confidence and Skill in Driving a Large Pick-Up Truck or Passenger Van Required to Accompany Rotations on Overnight Trips to Upstate Farms About The College of Veterinary Medicine at Long Island University: www.liu.edu/vetmed (http://www.liu.edu/vetmed) LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 46 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like Team Lead Animal Caretaker - Yaphank... #4861 Veterinary Clinical Sciences Licensed Veterinary Technician... #4839 Veterinary Clinical Sciences © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
