    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5013": {
      "title": "Success Coach and Greek Life Coordinator",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Success Coach and Greek Life Coordinator Success Coach and Greek Life Coordinator No. 5013 Long Island University Brookville, New York Center for Student Success and Coaching-Brookville Posted Sep 03, 2026 $66,300 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $66,300 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 03, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary The Success Coach and Greek Life Coordinator serves as a central resource in advancing student success, retention, and experiential learning at Long Island University. From orientation to graduation, this integrated role combines proactive, individualized coaching with the coordination of academic, career, and co-curricular support services to ensure students thrive throughout their LIU journey. Acting as a student’s primary point of contact, the Success Coach provides personalized guidance in academic planning, financial aid navigation, campus engagement, and career readiness. Coaches work one-on-one with students to develop tailored success plans aligned with their goals, interests, and strengths while supporting course selection, major exploration, scholarship access, internship guidance, study abroad opportunities, and post-graduation planning. In addition to direct student support, the Coordinator contributes to the operational and programmatic efforts that enhance the student experience, including leadership development initiatives, career workshops, and campus life programming. This dual function ensures a holistic approach to student development and supports the university’s broader goals of persistence, completion, and career success. Reporting to an Associate Director, Success Coaches may focus on key populations such as undergraduate students, graduate students, or international students, while attributing to residence life or campus life. Key Responsibilities Serve as the primary advisor and success coach for an assigned caseload of students, providing individualized support for academic, personal, and professional development. Guide students through the LIU Four-Year Model, from pre-enrollment and orientation through graduation, helping them integrate into the academic, social, and cultural life of the University. Support students with course registration, major selection, and degree planning aligned with their long-term career goals. Interpret career assessment tools and coach students in developing career paths that complement their academic pursuits. Assist students in navigating financial aid processes, including reviewing award information and understanding deadlines, procedures, and funding options. Plan and implement student success programming, including life planning seminars, academic workshops, and campus engagement initiatives that foster belonging and holistic development. Provide leadership in a designated area of academic success, campus life, residence life, and financial success. Collaborate with key departments across campus including but not limited to Admissions, Academic Affairs, Alumni and Employer Engagement, The Honors College, Learning Support Services, Athletics, to support recruitment, engagement, and retention strategies. Monitor student progress and maintain accurate records, submitting regular reports on retention, registration, and coaching outcomes. Support pre-enrollment and transition activities such as admissions events, orientation, and four-year programming. Perform other duties as assigned by the Associate Directors and Director of the Center for Student Success & Coaching. Ancillary Responsibilities (Fraternity and Sorority Life Focused) Advise fraternity and sorority chapters and governing councils – supporting leadership, operations, and goal setting. Coordinate, plan and execute formal and informal recruitment efforts with Panhellenic and Interfraternity councils. Advise and support Greek honor societies, including Order of Omega, Gamma Sigma Alpha, and Rho Lambda, Oversee chapter compliance with university policies, national standards, and risk management protocols. Coordinate leadership training, new member education, and educational workshops on topics such as hazing prevention, wellness, and inclusion, etc. Manage event registration and support safe planning of social, philanthropic, and recruitment events. Promote academic success, service, and campus involvement within the fraternity/sorority community. Track chapter performance, including membership data, GPA reports, and conduct records. Collaborate with campus partners and national headquarters to ensure holistic student support and community development. Respond to incidents and student concerns, connecting students to appropriate campus resources. Provide weekend and evening coverage of student life and student organization programs. Minimum Requirements Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s preferred. At least 1-3 years of progressively increasing experience in higher education, student affairs; sound judgment and decision-making skills. Excellent oral and written communication skills High energy and enthusiasm to work with students and propel them toward success Ability to design and implement innovative programs with a strong attention to detail Interpersonal communication skills Computer skills/literacy Working Conditions Flexible hours, including weekends and evenings, are required to execute this position including office and university events. Occasional travel to/from other LIU campuses for the facilitation of trainings, meetings and other university functions. Materials & Equipment Computer, Microsoft Suite, PeopleSoft, Texting Platform, copier, phone LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, marital or veteran status, or Vietnam-era veteran status, or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 46 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like Associate Director of Campus Life ... #5014 Center for Student Success and Coaching-Brookville © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
