    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5007": {
      "title": "FWS - Student Worker - Model United Nations Assistant",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU FWS - Student Worker - Model United Nations Assistant FWS - Student Worker - Model United Nations Assistant No. 5007 Long Island University Brookville, New York The Roosevelt School Posted Sep 02, 2026 $17.00/hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17.00/hour Start Date 08/31/2026 FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 02, 2026 Contact Gregory Barton, Dean, Roosevelt School Job Description Purpose or Role of the Position within the Organization\nBasic Function and Scope of Responsibilities: The Roosevelt School is seeking a dedicated and motivated LIU student to serve as a Model United Nations Assistant at the Post Campus. The Model UN Assistant will support the Model United Nations program in its student engagement, recruitment, programming, training, travel, and administrative activities.\nWorking closely with the Model UN Faculty Advisor and the Roosevelt School Dean, the Model UN Assistant will serve as an important point of support for LIU Model UN students and contribute to the growth and visibility of the program across the University.\nThis position provides an opportunity for a student to develop valuable skills in research, communication, event planning, student engagement, organizational management, and international affairs while gaining practical experience supporting one of LIU's student leadership and experiential learning programs. Responsibilities\nThe Model United Nations Assistant will: •\nMeet and coordinate regularly with the LIU Model UN Faculty Advisor regarding program activities, student needs, recruitment, training, travel, and upcoming events. •\nMeet and coordinate with LIU Model UN students when approached to provide support with research, writing, preparation, and travel arrangements. •\nAssist students in identifying resources and preparing for Model UN conferences and related activities. •\nPlan, promote, and attend LIU Model UN recruitment activities designed to attract new students to the program. •\nPlan, promote, and attend LIU Model UN promotional activities and events. •\nPlan, promote, and attend LIU Model UN fundraising activities. •\nRepresent LIU Model UN as an office-holder at Student Government Association (SGA) sessions, as appropriate. •\nAttend LIU Model UN training sessions and assist with program logistics and student support. •\nAssist with the coordination and promotion of Model UN meetings, workshops, training sessions, and other program activities. • Update and maintain the LIU Model UN website with current information,\nannouncements, events, photographs, and other approved content. • Assist with social media and other promotional communications related to Model UN\nactivities, as directed. • Help maintain organized records and materials related to Model UN activities, events,\nrecruitment, and travel. • Serve as a positive ambassador for LIU Model UN and the Roosevelt School when\ninteracting with students, faculty, staff, and external organizations. • Support the Model UN Faculty Advisor and Roosevelt School Dean with special projects\nand other program-related assignments as needed. Education Requirements: • LIU student currently enrolled in an active degree program. Training, Skills, Knowledge, and Experience : • Strong interest in international relations, diplomacy, political science, global affairs, or a\nrelated field. • Previous participation in Model United Nations is strongly preferred. • Strong written and verbal communication skills. • Strong research and writing skills. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail. • Ability to work independently while also collaborating effectively with students, faculty,\nand staff. • Ability to manage multiple responsibilities and meet deadlines. • Professional and interpersonal skills appropriate for representing LIU Model UN at\nUniversity and external events. • Familiarity with website content management systems and/or social media platforms is\npreferred. • Experience with event planning, student organizations, recruitment, fundraising, or\nstudent leadership is preferred. • Reliable and punctual, with a positive and proactive attitude. • Commitment to supporting an inclusive and welcoming student organization. Rate of Pay: $17.00/hour Period of Employment: 08/30/2026 - 05/30/2027 Evaluation Procedures and Schedules: The Model United Nations Assistant will be evaluated throughout the academic year to ensure\nstrong performance, professional growth, and alignment with the goals of the LIU Model UN\nprogram and the Roosevelt School.\nStudents will be assessed in the following areas: • Reliability and punctuality • Professionalism and communication • Research and writing support • Task accuracy and follow-through\n• Initiative and engagement • Event and program support • Collaboration with students, faculty, and staff • Representation of LIU Model UN and the Roosevelt School The evaluation process is developmental and designed to help the student build transferable\nskills in leadership, communication, organization, research, event management, and professional\nengagement. Equal Opportunity Employer LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunities in\nemployment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our\nacademic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard\nto race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or\nexpression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or\nmilitary status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal\nlaws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 47 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
