    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4917": {
      "title": "FWS Student Orientation Leader",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU FWS Student Orientation Leader FWS Student Orientation Leader No. 4917 Long Island University Brookville, New York Student Orientation Posted Sep 01, 2026 $400 one time payment Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $400 one time payment Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non Exempt Application Deadline Nov 30, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Job\nTitle: Orientation\nLeader Job\nType: FWS Student Worker Start\nDate: August 24,\n2026 Application\nDeadline: June 30, 2026 Salary\nRange: Stipend FLSA\nStatus: Exempt Contact: Post-StudentSuccess@liu.edu Full/Part\nTime: N/A Is\nthis a Federal Work Study position? YES Reports\nTo: Associate Director of Campus Life Basic\nFunction and Scope of Responsibilities: The Orientation\nLeader (OL) is a FWD student leader who serves as a welcoming and supportive peer\nmentor for incoming Long Island University students and their families during\nOrientation programs and Admissions events. OLs play a vital role in creating a\npositive first impression of LIU by helping new students feel connected,\ninformed, and excited to join Shark Nation. OLs are\nresponsible for assisting with Orientation programming, facilitating small\ngroup discussions and activities, supporting event logistics, and serving as a\nresource to new students throughout the transition process. This position is\ndesigned for enthusiastic student leaders who are passionate about student\nengagement, school spirit, and helping others. Key\nResponsibilities: · Welcome and assist new students and\nfamilies during First Year, Transfer, and Graduate Orientation programs · Serve as a positive representative\nof Long Island University · Facilitate icebreakers, group\ndiscussions, and engagement activities · Assist with event set-up, check-in,\nand event management · Provide accurate information\nregarding campus resources, student involvement, academic support, and campus\nlife · Support the Center for Student\nSuccess & Coaching throughout the year at Admissions Open Houses and\nAdmitted Students Days · Help foster an inclusive, welcoming,\nand engaging environment for all students · Maintain professionalism,\nconfidentiality, and strong communication Education\nRequirements: · Must be a currently enrolled LIU\nstudent in good academic and disciplinary standing Qualified\napplicants will have: · Strong communication and\ninterpersonal skills · Ability to work in a fast-paced,\nteam-oriented environment · Positive attitude, flexibility, and\nenthusiasm for helping others · Demonstrated involvement in campus\nlife and student engagement preferred Required\nDates & Commitments: · Leadership experience · Public speaking or presentation\nexperience · Ability to engage and connect with\ndiverse groups of students · Problem-solving and customer service\nskills Required\nDates & Commitments: All OLs are\nrequired to attend the following dates: · Orientation Leader Training: August\n24th – August 28th · First Year Move In: August 29th · New Student Orientation: August 30th\n– August 31st · Transfer & Graduate Student\nOrientation: September 1st Please note\nthat attendance Orientation dates are mandatory. Working\nConditions: Flexible hours,\nincluding weekends and evenings, are required to properly execute the position’s\nrole. Travel to/from other LIU campuses for the facilitation of training,\nmeetings and other university functions is required. LIU is an equal\nopportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunities in\nemployment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and\nexcellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all\nqualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic\ninformation, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression,\nmarital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status,\nveteran or military status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by\napplicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to\nwork in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 47 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
