    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5000": {
      "title": "Director of Sponsored Programs",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Director of Sponsored Programs Director of Sponsored Programs No. 5000 Long Island University Brookville, New York Intl Relation & Diplomacy Post Posted Sep 01, 2026 $120,000 - $150,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $120,000 - $150,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Nov 30, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary Long Island University seeks an experienced and collaborative Director of Sponsored Programs to provide strategic leadership for the University's growing research enterprise. Reporting to the Vice President of Research, the Director oversees sponsored programs administration, with primary responsibility for pre-award operations, research administration, and regulatory compliance. The Director partners with faculty, deans, and university leadership to increase external funding, strengthen research infrastructure, and advance LIU's strategic goal of becoming a nationally recognized R1 research university. This position supervises Office of Sponsored Programs staff and ensures exceptional customer service while maintaining compliance with federal, state, sponsor, and institutional requirements. Key Responsibilities Provide leadership for the University's sponsored programs administration and serve as the Executive Director's designee when assigned. Oversee pre-award and post-award administration, including proposal review, budget development, institutional approvals, sponsor submissions, and grant management. Supervise and mentor OSP staff, fostering a collaborative, service-oriented environment. Advise faculty on funding opportunities, proposal development, sponsor requirements, and institutional policies. Ensure compliance with Uniform Guidance (2 CFR Part 200), federal regulations, sponsor policies, and University procedures. Coordinate the submission of complex, multidisciplinary, and multi-institutional proposals. Develop and implement policies, procedures, templates, and best practices to improve research administration. Develop and deliver training programs for faculty and staff on grants administration and sponsor requirements. Monitor sponsored programs activity, prepare reports for University leadership, and support strategic research initiatives. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree from an accredited institution. Managerial experience in sponsored programs administration within higher education or a research institution. Demonstrated knowledge of federal research regulations, including Uniform Guidance (2 CFR Part 200), and major sponsors such as NIH, NSF, DOD, DOE, and HRSA. Strong organizational, analytical, communication, and leadership skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment while providing outstanding customer service. Preferred Qualifications PhD or similar doctoral degree. Certified Research Administrator (CRA) or related professional certification. Experience supporting research growth at an R1 or emerging research university. Experience with electronic research administration systems such as PeopleSoft, Cayuse, InfoEd, or Workday Why Long Island University? Long Island University is investing in research, innovation, and graduate education as it advances toward Carnegie R1 status. The Director of Sponsored Programs will play a key leadership role in expanding external funding, strengthening research infrastructure, and supporting faculty scholarship across the University. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 48 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5004": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean - School of Business",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Assistant Dean - School of Business Assistant Dean - School of Business No. 5004 Long Island University Brookville, New York Dean-College of Management Posted Sep 01, 2026 $90,001-$95,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $90,001-$95,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 01, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary The Assistant Dean is responsible for assisting and supporting the Dean in planning, coordinating, managing and monitoring, and evaluating all functions and activities associated with students, faculty, administrative personnel, programs, and associated operations in the School of Business. The incumbent serves as the representative of the Dean in assigned areas and in the Dean’s absence. The Assistant Dean supports program planning, outcomes assessment processes, professional development, and recruitment for the College. Strong communications, Excel and technology skills are required, and the incumbent must have a working knowledge of university financial management policies, procedures, and reporting. He/she must be able to work well with a diverse group of individuals, both inside and outside the School, including undergraduate and graduate students, full-time and adjunct faculty, administrative personnel at campus and university levels, parents, and outside agencies. Flexible hours, including weekends and evenings, are required to execute the position’s role responsibly. Key Responsibilities Implement and monitor programs, policies, and resource applications necessary to accomplish the mission, goals, and objectives of the School. Works with chair and faculty to finalize course schedules and teaching assignments, ensures full workloads for Full-Time Faculty, and approves all workloads before being sent to Payroll. Provide students mentorship and supports them with class enrollment and plan of study questions. Works with the Dean and other support areas to organize development and career service events. Participates in recruiting events, including high school visits, business competitions, LIU open houses, and additional events as needed. Continuously implement recruiting activities to increase enrollment for undergraduate and graduate students, including reaching out to prospective students and potential partnerships. Support extra-curricular clubs and activities related to the Business school, such as LIUiQ Consulting, LIU-investment fund, and LIU marketing society. Evaluates graduate admissions applications for Dean’s consideration. Reviews and provides feedback regarding budget plans and the management thereof to support the effective use of University resources. With the assistance of students and co-workers, be responsible for maintaining the COM website and the academic bulletins current and up to date. Completes surveys and required paperwork to augment the College’s status, including US News and World Report and the Princeton Review. Manage the Business School’s social media channels. 1 Assists with researching and writing miscellaneous and ad hoc reports/projects as needed. Additional duties as assigned. Minimum Requirements An earned Master’s degree in Business, Education, or a related field. Background in an educational setting is preferred. Skilled in Microsoft Office, particularly Excel, and PPT. Will work as part of the College of Management Dean’s Office team and must be able to work collegially Office setting on campus; in some instances, travel will be required for recruitment purposes. About the LIU School of Business The School of Business offers progressive, engaged learning to students, including LIU-iQ, the student consulting firm, LIU-iF, the student investment club, a thought-leadership lectures series, and professors from the top universities in the United States.  The College fosters the entrepreneurial spirit and embraces market-driven. From the shores of Long Island to the epicenter of business and tech innovation in Brooklyn to the far corners of the world, LIU offers a unique college experience for every student seeking academic enrichment and professional opportunity. Upon graduation, our students join a community of more than 265,000 alumni to become global leaders in fields that include the arts, health sciences, media, education, pharmacy, business, technology, public service, and professional sports. LIU is an equal-opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 48 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5005": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (NTTA), Game Design and Development",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Assistant Professor (NTTA), Game Design and Development Assistant Professor (NTTA), Game Design and Development No. 5005 Long Island University Brookville, New York Design & Digital Technology Posted Sep 01, 2026 $76,971 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Faculty Salary Range $76,971 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 01, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary Long Island University is seeking an experienced and talented full-time faculty NTTA member to join our illustrious digital game design and development program. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses, mentor students, and contribute to the development of a dynamic and experimental game design curriculum and culture. Relevant areas of expertise may include (but are not limited to): Gameplay programming, Game production, 2D/3D art and animation, Music and sound design, Spatial and interaction design and UI/UX design. Key Responsibilities Teaching a wide range of classes (introductory and advanced game development , gameplay programming, studio) Developing a curriculum to reflect current industry standards and emerging trends Mentoring and advising students on academic progress and portfolio development Supporting student projects, including capstones and collaborative team based work Participating in departmental meetings, curriculum planning, and faculty advisory boards Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Game Design, Interactive Media, Digital Media, or a related field (or equivalent professional experience) Varied and deep portfolio of published games Strong understanding of game systems, and mastery in a variety of gameplay engines Teaching experience at the college level Please submit the following with your application : Cover letter, Curriculum vitae (CV) or résumé, Teaching philosophy statement, Portfolio of game design work, Sample syllabi of previously taught classes, Contact information for [2–3] professional references. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunities in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 48 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Faculty Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
