    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/5001": {
      "title": "Secretary Level 6 - Local 153",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Secretary Level 6 - Local 153 Secretary Level 6 - Local 153 No. 5001 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Dean-Business Administration Posted Aug 31, 2026 $54,299 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Staff Salary Range $54,299 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Nov 30, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary Assists with the day-to-day running of the Dean's Office supporting School of Business and RocNation School of Music, Sports and Entertainment. Responsibilities Serves as initial face-to-face and telephone contact point for students, faculty members and outside visitors. Each semester collects Outside Additional Professional Activities forms, syllabi, research and service summaries along with other required documents or materials. Assist students/ faculty/staff in getting documentation needed in connection with student registrations, change of grades, VISA forms, permission codes, etc. Coordinates department faculty recruitment efforts and records. Assures that proper forms and expenses are submitted in a timely manner, makes appointments and reservations, as necessary. Assists with department research projects, as relevant. Prepares and processes required electronic filing of workloads, each semester. Assists in organizing Honor Society inductions, Commencement, Awards and other events, as needed (some hours outside 9am to 5pm, M-F may be required on rare occasion). Assists in scheduling appointments, typing up correspondence. Makes appointments and schedules virtual meetings, as requested. Orders department supplies and keeps supply cabinet and storage areas neat. Overall responsibility for physical mail. Collects mail daily, make sure outgoing mail is picked up. Each semester, set up mail boxes for all current Deans, Faculty and Staff. Maintains college's lists including, telephone list, room list, adjunct faculty list, along with faculty and adjunct CVs, etc. Assists in a wide variety of projects as requested. Other duties as required by the Dean. Minimum Requirements Working knowledge of Microsoft Word, Excel, Outlook, Microsoft Teams and otherwise internet/computer savvy. Experience working in a professional environment. Special Information: Salary: *In accordance with Local 153 guidelines LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable local, state, or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 49 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Staff Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
