    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4996": {
      "title": "Director of Assessment and Accreditation",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Director of Assessment and Accreditation Director of Assessment and Accreditation No. 4996 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Executive Dean Pharmacy Posted Aug 28, 2026 $90,000 - $95,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $90,000 - $95,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Nov 28, 2026 Contact Please complete online application Job Description Position Summary: The Long Island University Arnold and Marie Schwartz College of Pharmacy and Health\nSciences (LIU Pharmacy) invites applications for the position of Director of Assessment and\nAccreditation. This leadership role is responsible for assessment and accreditation activities for the\nPharmD and graduate programs. The Director collaborates with faculty, staff, and administrators to\ndesign and execute assessment strategies that measure learning outcomes, program effectiveness, and\nstakeholder satisfaction. The role ensures the alignment of the College’s assessment activities with the\nUniversity institutional effectiveness requirements as well as programmatic and regional accreditation\nstandards, with a focus on continuous quality improvement of all programs. The position reports to the\nDean of the College of Pharmacy. Duties and Responsibilities : Oversee a comprehensive assessment plan for the PharmD program, ensuring alignment with\npolicies and accreditation standards (e.g., ACPE, university, state, or regional accrediting bodies). Oversee a comprehensive assessment plan for graduate programs, ensuring alignment with\nCollege and University accreditations standards. Provide leadership in the collection, analysis, and reporting of data to support strategic\nplanning, program improvement, student services, admissions, and decision-making. Oversee the AACP Institutional Effectiveness surveys and report outcomes to the Administrative\nteam and faculty for action items. Manage the Strategic Plan process, ensuring that all stakeholders participate in the collection of\ndata to inform the accomplishments of strategic initiatives. Serve as a resource on assessment and quality enhancement practices\n Collaborate with faculty and staff to design and implement assessment tools that evaluate\nstudent learning outcomes and curricular effectiveness. Oversee the development, distribution, and analysis of surveys, exams, rubrics, and other\nassessment instruments. Maintain a database of assessment results and ensure data integrity, security, and accessibility\nfor stakeholders. Work with the Dean and the Administrative team to prepare and manage documentation for\naccreditation self-studies, site visits, and reports. Analyze assessment data to identify trends, gaps, and opportunities for improvement in\ncurriculum and program delivery and compliance with ACPE standards. Facilitate discussions and planning sessions with faculty, staff, and administrators to promote a\nculture of evidence-based decision-making. Represent the College of Pharmacy on University-level committees related to assessment and\naccreditation. Stay current on trends and advancements in pharmacy and higher education assessment and\naccreditation. Requirements: The successful candidate must hold a Masters Degree or doctoral degree (MS, PhD, PharmD,\nEdD, or equivalent) Experience in assessment, institutional effectiveness, or related areas, preferably in a pharmacy\nor health sciences educational setting Knowledge of national or programmatic accreditation standards and reporting procedures. Proficiency in data collection, analysis, and reporting. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Familiarity with survey software (e.g., Qualtrics), statistical tools (e.g., SPSS, SAS, or R), and\nvisualization platforms (e.g., Tableau or Power BI), Learning Management Systems, ExamSoft,\nand Enflux is desirable. About LIU Brooklyn: LIU\nBrooklyn campus enables students to realize their full potential as\nethically grounded, intellectually vigorous, and socially responsible global\ncitizens. The campus offers more professional programs in health care than any\nother campus in the New York metropolitan area, including the Arnold and Marie\nSchwartz College of Pharmacy & Health Science, and The Harriet Rothkopf\nHeilbrunn School of Nursing. LIU Brooklyn is home to Kumble Theater for the\nPerforming Arts, a dynamic performance venue designed to nourish students’\nartistic exploration, and Division I sports teams. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 52 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4997": {
      "title": "Head Coach - Women's Golf",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Head Coach - Women's Golf Head Coach - Women's Golf No. 4997 Long Island University Brookville, New York Women's Golf Posted Aug 28, 2026 $50,000 - $55,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $50,000 - $55,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Nov 28, 2026 Contact complete online application Job Description Position Summary: LIU is seeking a highly motivated and experienced individual to lead its NCAA Division I Women’s Golf program. Reporting to the Director of Athletics, this full-time position, based on the Post campus, is responsible for the overall direction, leadership, and development of the golf programs. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to building a competitive and inclusive team culture, fostering the academic and athletic success of student-athletes, and upholding the values and standards of LIU Athletics. Key Responsibilities: Oversee personnel and budgeting for the women’s golf programs. Serve as head coach, and direct all aspects of the women’s golf program, including training, game planning, and competitive performance. Recruit, evaluate, and retain student-athletes who embody the academic and athletic standards of LIU. Support student-athlete development on and off the court, including academic success, leadership, and well-being. Ensure program compliance with all NCAA, Northeast Conference (NEC), and LIU regulations and policies. Oversee the management of the women’s golf team operations, including (but not limited to) budget, travel, scheduling, and equipment. Hire, supervise, and develop assistant coaches and support staff. Coordinate scouting, video breakdown, and opponent preparation. Engage with alumni, campus departments, and community partners to promote the program. Foster a culture of accountability, integrity, and mutual respect within the team. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred. Minimum of 3–5 years of successful collegiate coaching experience, preferably at the NCAA Division I level. Demonstrated success in recruiting and developing student-athletes. Strong understanding of NCAA rules and regulations. Excellent leadership, organizational, and communication skills. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and travel as required. About LIU Post: LIU Post campus is a scenic, historic, and\nscholarly campus that offers a small-school environment with the access and\nresources of a major metropolitan university. The University's 350+ acre campus\nis located on the estate of Marjorie Merriweather Post, 27 miles east of New\nYork City on Long Island's Gold Coast. The campus houses the Lewyt College of\nVeterinary Medicine, the first professional School of Accountancy, an\nAACSB-accredited Business School, and an award-winning theater program. LIU is\nhome to the world-renowned Tilles Center for the Performing Arts and the Shark\nStadium, where supporters gather to cheer on the Sharks’ Division I athletic\nprogram. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is\ncommitted to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can\ncontribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. We encourage\napplications from all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, religion, genetic information,\nsexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin,\nethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other basis\nprotected by applicable laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 52 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4998": {
      "title": "Women’s Ice Hockey – Equipment/Operations Manager Position",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Women’s Ice Hockey – Equipment/Operations Manager Position Women’s Ice Hockey – Equipment/Operations Manager Position No. 4998 Long Island University Brookville, New York Athletics - Womens Ice Hockey Posted Aug 28, 2026 $20,000 - $25,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $20,000 - $25,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Nov 28, 2026 Contact complete online application Job Description Position Summary: The Equipment/Operations Manager (Full-Time position) is responsible for managing all equipment-related duties pertaining to the LIU Women’s Ice Hockey Team and will report directly to the Head Coach. Duties include managing and creating equipment/apparel order(s), laundry, maintenance and repair of athletic equipment & apparel, inventory of athletic equipment, distribution and fitting of equipment and apparel, assisting with equipment inspection and reconditioning and assisting with team meal orders/snacks at home and on away trips. Responsibilities: Daily practice set up (towels, jerseys, socks, loops, sport drinks, water, etc.) Pre-practice skate sharpening, equipment repairs (sewing, etc.) and equipment modifications Pre-practice bench set up: water bottles, coaches board, tape, sticks, cones, etc. Post-practice skate sharpening, equipment repairs, equipment modification, equipment replacement, equipment cleaning, and laundry All general housekeeping duties for the locker room Game day set up: home team dressing room, visitors dressing room, and referees’ room (in accordance with league rules) Lead communication prior to road trips with opponent’s rink admin and/or equipment manager to ensure we are prepared prior to making the trip On road trips, coordinate with bus driver for personal transportation to/from the rink in order to execute locker room duties while on the road Develop/maintain contacts within the league for the purpose of becoming familiar with arena regulations and set up Manage in-season and post-season inventory of all hockey equipment, supplies, apparel, etc. Keep and maintain effective and accurate records of equipment/apparel ordered; all final orders through vendors may only be placed by the Head Coach Assist in setting up and cleaning up team meals and snacks Preferred Qualifications: Candidate must demonstrate strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills with the ability to develop and maintain effective relationships with both internal and external personnel. Candidate must demonstrate the ability to communicate effectively in writing. Candidate must also possess strong organizational and time management skills with the ability to prioritize and manage multiple tasks, and the ability to work a non-standard work week.\nAbilities and Skills: Must know how to skate sharpen Must know how to make skate repairs (replacement, riveting, eyelets, punching,\nuse of oven) Must know how to sew Ability to make effective modifications Ability to keep, maintain, and prepare effective and accurate records Ability to maintain effective relationships with management, league officials, facility\nrepresentatives, the media, fellow employees, and the general public Proficient in Microsoft Office and Google Sheets About LIU Post: LIU Post campus is a scenic, historic, and\nscholarly campus that offers a small-school environment with the access and\nresources of a major metropolitan university. The University's 350+ acre campus\nis located on the estate of Marjorie Merriweather Post, 27 miles east of New\nYork City on Long Island's Gold Coast. The campus houses the Lewyt College of\nVeterinary Medicine, the first professional School of Accountancy, an\nAACSB-accredited Business School, and an award-winning theater program. LIU is\nhome to the world-renowned Tilles Center for the Performing Arts and the Shark\nStadium, where supporters gather to cheer on the Sharks’ Division I athletic\nprogram. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal\nopportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the\ndiversity and excellence of our academic community. We encourage applications\nfrom all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, religion, genetic information,\nsexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital or parental status,\nnational origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age,\ndisability, or any other basis protected by applicable laws. Hiring is contingent on\neligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 52 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4040": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Tenure Track Professor-Clinical Psychology Doctoral Program",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Assistant/Associate Tenure Track Professor-Clinical Psychology Doctoral Program Assistant/Associate Tenure Track Professor-Clinical Psychology Doctoral Program No. 4040 Long Island University Brookville, New York Psychology Doctoral Program (Post) Posted Aug 27, 2026 $98,001-$128,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Faculty Salary Range $98,001-$128,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Nov 27, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description The School of Health Professions at Long Island University ( LIU ) Post\ncampus is seeking applicants for a tenure track assistant professor position\nin the Clinical Psychology Doctoral Program (PsyD).  The\nposition involves teaching and supervising research in PsyD course sequences. A\nsuccessful candidate must be able to participate in department- and university-level\ncommittees, establish an extramurally funded research program that involves\nstudents, and supervise student practicum experiences. Applicants must\nhave a PhD or equivalent in psychology and have a New York State License in\nPsychology. Applicants should have a strong record of excellence in teaching\nand scholarly activity, including peer-reviewed research and grant writing, and\nshow enthusiasm to continue growing the academic, research, and clinical\ntraining aspects of the Psy.D. program. Applicants should have a commitment to\nfree and open discourse as a core value of learning. This posting represents\nmultiple openings. Preference will be given to applicants with expertise in\ncognitive-behavioral therapy, dialectical behavior therapy , and/or\ntransdiagnostic approaches. Preference will be given to applicants with expertise in severe\nand persistent mental illness. Please submit: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement (with evidence of effectiveness) Statement of Research Interests Reprints/Preprints of peer-reviewed research Names, email addresses, and telephone numbers of three academic\n     references Principal Responsibility Teaching\nresponsibilities: · Teaching\ndoctoral level clinical psychology coursework, preference: · candidates\nwho can teach DBT courses. · candidates\nwho can teach courses in Severe and Persistent Mental Illness (SMI) · candidates\nwho can teach assessments, specifically: MMI-3 and Rorschach-Exner system. · Academic\nadvisement · Engagement\nin departmental activities and events · Clinical\nsupervision · Dissertation\nmentoring LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 52 Days Since Posted 4 Positions Available Faculty Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4099": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate Professor-NTTA for Nutrition Programs",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Assistant / Associate Professor-NTTA for Nutrition Programs Assistant / Associate Professor-NTTA for Nutrition Programs No. 4099 Long Island University Brookville, New York Nutrition Posted Aug 27, 2026 $76,971 - $84,557 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Faculty Salary Range $76,971 - $84,557 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Nov 30, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Position Summary: The\nSchool of Health Professions is seeking a full time, non-tenure track professor\nto teach in the undergraduate Didactic Program in Dietetics and the graduate\nMS/RDN professional program with potential to assume Program Director role. Key Responsibilities: Contribute to management and administration of\naccredited programs. Teach 24 credits per academic year in the BS and MS/RDN nutrition\nprograms. Participate in departmental, school and campus committees as appointed. Engage in departmental and campus recruitment events. Promote student retention. Contribute to curriculum development and evaluation Participate in all Departmental, School, and Campus committees (as\nappointed). Engage in Departmental and Campus recruitment efforts. Maintain high academic standards utilizing appropriate student evaluation\nmechanisms for assigned courses/programs; analyze and implement\nchanges as part of these programmatic and Departmental outcomes Have a master of science degree, be credentialed as a Registered Dietitian\nNutritionist by the Commission on Dietetic Registration and have three\nyears of professional experience post credentialing. Training, Skills, Knowledge, Experience: College-level teaching and administrative experience in a baccalaureate or\nhigher degree program. Excellent skills in leadership, supervision, written and oral communication\nskills. Working Conditions: Office setting on campus Materials & Equipme