    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/3586": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor for Nutrition Programs",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Adjunct Professor for Nutrition Programs Adjunct Professor for Nutrition Programs No. 3586 Long Island University Brookville, New York Nutrition Posted Aug 27, 2026 $1,000-$1,350 per credit Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Adjunct Faculty Salary Range $1,000-$1,350 per credit Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Feb 26, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Long Island University (LIU Post) is seeking a pplicants interested in adjunct professor positions in programs within undergraduate and graduate Nutrition Programs. Courses may include : Graduate Electives, Undergraduate Advanced Nutrition, Undergraduate and Graduate Food Services courses. Basic Function and Scope of Responsibilities: Responsible for the instruction, supervision and evaluation of students in the classroom and/or laboratory setting. Providing instruction in accordance with established curriculum, course outlines and class schedules. Creating and maintaining an environment which emphasizes learning, encourages free discussion of ideas and critical thinking. Maintaining appropriate standards of professional conduct and ethics. Maintaining current knowledge in the subject matter areas. Fulfilling professional responsibilities of a part-time/temporary faculty member. Prepare a syllabus for each course taught using the college template and post it to the class on the Blackboard site. Teach class in a professional manner, teaching the material that is present in the syllabus and course outline. Advise students relative to their academic status or performance. Appropriately maintain all necessary records for each course taught. Cultivate in oneself and others an attitude of helpfulness, personal commitment to building relationships, managing to the best solution, and user friendly always. Education /Training Requirements: Masters in nutrition , dietetics, dietetics and food administration or related field and certification as a registered dietitian nutritionist OR Doctoral degree in nutrition, dietetics, dietetics and food administration, public health, leadership or related field Salary:  $1,000-$1,350 per credit LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 53 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
