    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4994": {
      "title": "Dean of Lewyt College of Veterinary Medicine",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Dean of Lewyt College of Veterinary Medicine Dean of Lewyt College of Veterinary Medicine No. 4994 Long Island University Brookville, New York Dean - Veterinary Medicine Posted Aug 26, 2026 $340,000 - $350,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $340,000 - $350,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 31, 2026 Job Description POSITION\nSUMMARY Long Island\nUniversity (LIU) invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean\nof the Lewyt College of Veterinary Medicine (LCVM) . This is an exceptional\nopportunity to lead one of the nation's newest and most innovative colleges of\nveterinary medicine as it enters its next phase of growth, excellence, and\nnational prominence. The Dean serves\nas the chief academic and administrative officer of the College and provides\nvisionary leadership to advance excellence in veterinary education,\nscholarship, clinical partnerships, research, service, and innovation. The Dean\nwill lead a highly collaborative community of faculty, staff, students, alumni,\nand external partners while promoting an inclusive culture that prepares\ngraduates who are both career ready and future ready to lead the veterinary\nprofession. The successful\ncandidate will embrace innovation, foster interdisciplinary collaboration,\nsupport faculty and student success, advance research and scholarly activity, strengthen\npartnerships across the veterinary profession, animal health industries, and\nother stakeholders, and position the College as a national leader in veterinary\neducation. The Dean reports\nto the President of Long Island University and serves as a member of the\nUniversity's senior academic leadership team. LEADERSHIP\nRESPONSIBILITIES Strategic\nVision and Institutional Leadership The Dean will: Provide visionary leadership that\n     advances the mission, vision, and strategic priorities of the Lewyt\n     College of Veterinary Medicine. Lead development and\n     implementation of the College's strategic plan while identifying emerging\n     opportunities that position the College for national distinction. Foster a culture of innovation,\n     collaboration, accountability, excellence, and continuous improvement. Represent the College within the\n     University and to local, national, and international stakeholders. Sustain and build productive\n     relationships with veterinary organizations, industry, government\n     agencies, alumni, donors, philanthropic partners, and the community. Promote interdisciplinary\n     collaboration across Long Island University. Champion a culture of inclusion and\n     well-being throughout the College community. Academic\nExcellence The Dean will\nprovide leadership for: A high-quality, integrated Doctor\n     of Veterinary Medicine curriculum that meets the evolving needs of the\n     veterinary profession and society. Educational innovation utilizing\n     emerging technologies including artificial intelligence, simulation,\n     digital learning, and other evolving and emerging educational approaches\n     and technologies. Competency-based education. Pioneering  outcomes-focused assessment. Continuous curriculum review and\n     improvement. Establishing expectations for achievement\n     of faculty excellence in teaching, scholarship, mentoring, and service. Development of graduate education,\n     research opportunities, and continuing professional education. Accreditation\nand Quality Assurance The Dean will: Ensure achievement of all\n     standards for accreditation. Lead preparation for accreditation\n     reviews and reporting. Foster a culture of continuous\n     assessment and quality improvement. Utilize educational analytics and\n     performance metrics to guide strategic decision-making. Ensure compliance with all\n     university, state, and federal requirements. Faculty\nLeadership The Dean will: Lead recruitment, development,\n     mentorship, and retention of a world-class faculty. Enable faculty success in\n     teaching, scholarship, leadership, innovation, and clinical excellence. Encourage and facilitate interdisciplinary\n     research and collaboration. Support professional development\n     and leadership development opportunities. Foster a collegial culture that\n     values collaboration, transparency, integrity, and shared governance. Model inclusive team-based\n     healthcare delivery by establishing and leading a highly functioning team. Student\nSuccess The Dean will: Lead student recruitment,\n     retention, academic success, wellness, and professional development. Foster a student-centered\n     educational environment. Lead and development academic\n     programs that ensure future-ready graduates. Enable development of future\n     veterinary leaders committed to service, professionalism, communication,\n     and lifelong learning. Lead and support initiatives that\n     enhance student engagement and belonging. Research,\nInnovation, and Clinical Partnerships The Dean will: Lead advancement of research,\n     scholarship, and innovation throughout the College. Strengthen partnerships with\n     veterinary practices, specialty hospitals, industry, government agencies,\n     animal welfare organizations, and biomedical research institutions. Expand opportunities for\n     experiential and distributive clinical education. Promote translational research and\n     interdisciplinary collaborations. Position LCVM as a national leader\n     in veterinary educational innovation. Advancement\nand External Relations The Dean will: Partner with University\n     Advancement to increase philanthropic support. Cultivate relationships with\n     alumni, donors, foundations, corporations, and other friends of the\n     College. Serve as the primary ambassador\n     for the College. Enhance the College's visibility,\n     reputation, and national influence. Promote partnerships that support\n     education, research, innovation, and community engagement. Financial and\nAdministrative Leadership The Dean will: Establish a culture of\n     accountability and provide responsible stewardship of College resources. Develop and manage strategic and\n     operational budgets. Ensure effective planning,\n     resource allocation, and organizational effectiveness. Lead recruitment and development\n     of administrative leaders. Promote operational excellence and\n     continuous organizational improvement. Work effectively with University\n     Support Services. Required\nQualifications The successful\ncandidate will possess outstanding academic credentials and demonstrated\nleadership success, including: DVM, VMD, or equivalent veterinary\n     degree. Eligibility for appointment as a\n     tenured Professor. Record of distinguished academic\n     achievement in teaching, scholarship, and service. Significant senior leadership\n     experience in veterinary medical education or a comparable academic\n     environment. Demonstrated success leading\n     complex organizations through strategic planning and organizational\n     growth. Experience with accreditation and\n     continuous quality improvement. Strong record of faculty\n     development and mentorship. Excellent communication,\n     interpersonal, and relationship-building skills. Demonstrated commitment to\n     collaborative leadership and shared governance. Demonstrated commitment to a\n     culture of inclusion and belonging. Integrity. Preferred\nQualifications Preference will\nbe given to candidates with experience in one or more of the following: Advanced graduate degree (PhD or\n     equivalent). Veterinary specialty board\n     certification. Successful leadership of\n     innovative educational programs. Competency-based veterinary\n     education. Outcomes assessment and\n     educational analytics. Research administration. Fundraising and philanthropic\n     engagement. Clinical enterprise development. Artificial intelligence,\n     educational technology, and digital transformation. Strategic partnerships with\n     industry and the veterinary profession. Personal\nCharacteristics The successful\nDean will be: A visionary leader. An accomplished academic. An exceptional communicator. Collaborative, inclusive, and\n     transparent. Innovative and forward-thinking. Student-centered. Faculty-centered. Committed to excellence. Skilled at building consensus. Financially astute. Ethical, authentic, and\n     approachable. Passionate about advancing\n     veterinary medicine and veterinary education . About the\nLewyt College of Veterinary Medicine The Lewyt College\nof Veterinary Medicine at Long Island University is committed to educating the\nnext generation of veterinarians through innovation, collaboration, and\nexcellence. The College embraces modern educational practices, distributive\nclinical education, emerging technologies, and partnerships across the\nveterinary profession to prepare graduates who are equipped to lead in an\nincreasingly dynamic, team-based healthcare environment. Located on the\nLong Island University’s Post campus in Brookville, the College benefits from\naccess to one of the nation's largest and most diverse veterinary communities,\nworld-class biomedical research institutions, animal welfare organizations,\nspecialty referral centers, and proximity to New York City. Application\nProcess Applications\nshould include: Letter of interest describing\n     qualifications and leadership philosophy. Curriculum vitae. Statement of vision for the future\n     of veterinary medical education. Contact information for at least\n     five professional references. Review of\napplications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Long Island\nUniversity conducts background checks on all final candidates prior to\nemployment. Long Island\nUniversity is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to building a diverse\nacademic community and encourages applications from individuals who will\ncontribute to the excellence and inclusiveness of the University. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 53 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like Administrative Assistant - Research and Graduate S... #5028 Dean - Veterinary Medicine © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4664": {
      "title": "Adjunct Assistant Professor",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Adjunct Assistant Professor Adjunct Assistant Professor No. 4664 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Comm Science and Disorders (Brooklyn) Posted Aug 26, 2026 $1,000–$1,350 per credit Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Adjunct Faculty Salary Range $1,000–$1,350 per credit FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 25, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Adjunct Professor of Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences Position Summary: The Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders at LIU Brooklyn is seeking an\nAdjunct Professor to teach with experience in speech-language pathologist with advanced knowledge\nin the assessment, diagnosis, and treatment of swallowing disorders across the lifespan. The\ncourse should integrate evidence-based practice consideration of social determinants of health in\nclinical care. Key Responsibilities: • Develop and teach a graduate-level Dysphagia course for speech-language pathology\nstudents, ensuring alignment with current ASHA practice guidelines and CAA\naccreditation standards. • Incorporate case-based and problem-solving approaches that address pediatric and adult\nswallowing disorders • Highlight culturally and linguistically responsive practices in dysphagia management. • Collaborate with the Program Director to provide updates or materials that support\naccreditation reporting and curricular alignment. Qualifications: • Master’s degree in Speech-Language Pathology required; PhD or PhD candidacy in\nCommunication Sciences and Disorders preferred. • Current Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology (CCCSLP) from ASHA. • Demonstrated expertise in the assessment and treatment of swallowing disorders in\npediatric and/or adult populations. • A record of effective teaching at the graduate level in speech-language pathology or\nrelated fields. • Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with a commitment to fostering an\ninclusive and engaging educational environment. Salary Range: $1,000–$1,350 per Credit LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. We encourage applications from all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 54 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4935": {
      "title": "Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, Veterinary Medicine",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, Veterinary Medicine Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, Veterinary Medicine No. 4935 Long Island University Brookville, New York Veterinary Medicine Posted Aug 24, 2026 $180,000 - $200,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $180,000 - $200,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 31, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Position Summary The Associate Dean for Academic Affairs will provide strategic academic leadership to support and advance an accredited Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) program. Reporting to the Vice Dean for Academic Affairs, the Associate Dean is responsible for the coordination, oversight, and continuous enhancement of all academic aspects of the DVM program, from student recruitment through graduation. The successful candidate will champion LIU-CVM's mission to advance veterinary medical education through excellence in teaching, research, service, and innovation while ensuring graduates are prepared to meet the evolving needs of the veterinary profession and society. Key Responsibilities Academic Leadership Serve as a member of the University’s\n     senior leadership team. Provide leadership and oversight\n     for academic affairs in collaboration with the Vice Dean for Academic\n     Affairs, Vice Dean for Clinical Affairs, and the Academic and Clinical\n     Affairs teams. Ensure delivery of a\n     high-quality, integrated veterinary curriculum spanning foundational and\n     clinical education that aligns with the University’s mission, strategic\n     priorities, and accreditation requirements. Develop, implement, and oversee\n     academic policies and procedures, including matters related to student\n     academic standing. Foster collaboration among\n     faculty, academic departments, and clinical partners to promote\n     educational excellence. Curriculum Oversight and Innovation Chair the Curriculum Committee\n     and contribute to related academic committees. Lead ongoing curriculum review,\n     assessment, and continuous improvement initiatives. Evaluate curriculum effectiveness\n     through assessment outcomes, benchmarking, and stakeholder feedback. Coordinate curricular innovations\n     and revisions that address emerging veterinary workforce needs and\n     societal expectations. Promote the integration of\n     clinical reasoning, professional competencies, communication skills,\n     leadership development, well-being, and technology throughout the\n     curriculum. Advance innovative educational\n     strategies and emerging technologies that support effective teaching and\n     learning, particularly for adult learners. Accreditation and Regulatory\nCompliance Provide leadership in maintaining\n     compliance with accreditation standards established by the national\n     accrediting body for veterinary medical education. Coordinate accreditation\n     reporting, documentation, and site visit preparation. Ensure compliance with\n     university, state, federal, and professional requirements. Oversee assessment and\n     documentation of educational outcomes to support accreditation and quality\n     assurance efforts. Student Success and Academic Support Partner with Student Affairs\n     leadership to promote student success, retention, wellness, and\n     professional development. Oversee academic progression\n     policies, student performance review processes, and academic standing\n     procedures. Participate in student review and\n     academic standing committees as appropriate. Foster an inclusive, supportive,\n     and student-centered learning environment. Faculty Development and Engagement Support faculty excellence in\n     teaching, mentoring, scholarship, and service. Provide guidance and mentorship\n     related to curriculum design, outcomes-based education, educational\n     innovation, and veterinary education research. Promote faculty development\n     initiatives focused on teaching effectiveness, assessment practices,\n     educational technology, leadership, and professional growth. Cultivate a collaborative culture\n     of continuous learning and academic excellence. Assessment and Continuous Quality\nImprovement Lead the development, refinement,\n     and maintenance of assessment systems that support evaluation of student\n     achievement, courses, curriculum effectiveness, and institutional\n     outcomes. Collaborate with the Vice Dean\n     for Clinical Affairs to ensure rigorous evaluation of clinical education\n     quality, consistency, objectives, and outcomes. Utilize educational data,\n     analytics, and evidence-based practices to inform decision-making and\n     continuous improvement efforts. Develop and monitor key\n     performance indicators related to academic success, educational\n     effectiveness, and program quality. Work closely with Outcomes\n     Assessment to advance institutional assessment goals. Required Qualifications DVM, VMD, or equivalent\n     veterinary degree. Eligibility for appointment at\n     the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. Significant experience in\n     veterinary medical education. Demonstrated experience in\n     curriculum development, academic assessment, and academic administration. Strong leadership,\n     organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills. Proven ability to collaborate\n     effectively with diverse stakeholders. Preferred Qualifications PhD, additional doctoral degree,\n     and/or veterinary specialty board certification. Expertise in outcomes assessment\n     and continuous quality improvement. Experience with competency-based\n     veterinary education. Demonstrated success in\n     educational innovation and contemporary teaching and learning\n     methodologies. Commitment\nto fostering diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging within academic and\nprofessional environments. About The Lewyt College of Veterinary Medicine at Long Island University: LIU-LCVM received a Letter of Reasonable Assurance from the AVMA- Council on Education on October 16, 2019 and graduated its inaugural class in May 2024. Currently, with over 100 off-campus affiliate sites, LIU Lewyt College of Veterinary Medicine utilizes a distributed model of clinical education. The Lewyt College of Veterinary Medicine has modern physical facilities designed to support its instructional needs and research activities.\n\n\nwww.liu.edu/vetmed LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regards to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 56 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
