    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4990": {
      "title": "Federal Work-Study Student Worker- Center for Student Success",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Federal Work-Study Student Worker- Center for Student Success Federal Work-Study Student Worker- Center for Student Success No. 4990 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Center for Student Success and Coaching-Brooklyn Posted Aug 21, 2026 $17 an hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 an hour Start Date 08/01/2026 FLSA Status Non -Exempt Application Deadline Nov 12, 2026 Contact submit online application Job Description Basic Function and Scope of Responsibilities The Center for Student Success is seeking friendly, dependable, and customer service-oriented Federal Work\nStudy Student Workers to assist professional staff in supporting students, parents, faculty, staff, and campus\nvisitors in a fast-paced office environment. Student Workers will assist with providing general customer service\nby answering routine phone inquiries, responding to basic questions using approved resources and/or directing\ncallers to appropriate campus services. This position is designed to provide meaningful work experience while\ndeveloping communication, customer service, problem-solving, teamwork, and another professional workplace\nskills in a higher education environment. Principal Responsibilities Provide courteous and professional customer service to students, parents, faculty, staff, and visitors.\n• Assist students with navigating university websites and self-service resources.\n• Route calls and visitors to the appropriate department when additional assistance is needed.\n• Refer complex or sensitive questions to a Success Coach, Associate Director, or Director.\n• Maintain the confidentiality of student information in accordance with FERPA and University policies.\n• Perform other related duties as assigned. Education Requirements Must be a currently enrolled LIU student.\n• Must be awarded and eligible for the Federal Work-Study Program.\n• Must maintain Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP) in accordance with University and Federal Work-Study requirements. Working Conditions Student Workers will work in the Center for Student Success under the supervision of professional staff and\nassist with daily operations. Duties include answering telephones, assisting visitors, using a computer and office\nequipment, and providing customer service in a professional office environment. Materials & Equipment Student Workers will be provided with the equipment and resources necessary to perform their assigned duties,\nincluding a computer, telephone/headset, and access to University systems required for the position. Salary New York State Minimum Wage Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 58 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Closing Soon Applications close on Nov 12, 2026 © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
