      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Athletics Brooklyn Game Ops Athletics Brooklyn Game Ops No. 4987 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Athletics-General (Brooklyn) Posted Aug 21, 2026 $17.00 per hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17.00 per hour Start Date 08/01/2026 FLSA Status Non- Exempt Application Deadline Nov 12, 2026 Contact Michael Johnson Job Description Basic Function and Scope of Responsibilites: Assist with the setup, execution and breakdown of athletic events. Duties and Principal Responsibilities: Assist with the setup, execution and breakdown of athletic events.  Responsibilities include preparing competition venues by setting up scorer's tables, team benches, chairs, signage, game equipment, water stations, and hospitality areas; supporting game -day operations during events. Education Requirements: LIU student enrolled in an active degree program. Training, Skills, Knowledge, Experience: Period of Employment:  Begin: 08/01/2026 End: 06/30/2027 Evaluation procedures and schedules: Performance will be evaluated by the Game Operations staff based on attendance, punctuality, reliability, professionalism, initiative, teamwork, and successful completion of assigned game-day responsibilities.  This position works a flexible schedule based on athletic event needs, with a maximum of 17 hours per week. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable loc