    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4681": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Assessment Team Psychological Services Center",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Student Worker - Assessment Team Psychological Services Center Student Worker - Assessment Team Psychological Services Center No. 4681 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Psychology Doctoral Program (Brooklyn) Posted Aug 21, 2026 $17 per hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 per hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Jan 01, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Name of the position: Student Worker Is this a Federal Work Study position? Yes Classification of the position: Other Description : Campus: Brooklyn Department Name: Clinical Psychology Department’s Dean and/or Director: Meredith Kneavel Location: Building and Floor: Humanities 8 floor Supervisor: Name: Kevin Meehan Title: Program Director Purpose or role of the position within the organization\n(Basic Function and Scope of Responsibilities): STUDENT WORKER ASSESSMENT TEAM PSYCHOLOGICAL SERVICES CENTER Duties and Principal Responsibilities: Team Leader or Assistant Team Leader on Psychological Services Center Assessment Teams; Coordinate testing assignments and timeline for administration, scoring, interpretation, and reports; Review and provide feedback on test protocols and reports;Meet with Assessment Team on a weekly basis (2 hours per week);Facilitate communication between Assessment Teams and Advanced Assessment Course Provide individual supervision for Assessment Team members;Provide group inservice about testing procedures;Consult with Testing Supervisor and Director of Psychological Services Center; Education Requirements: LIU student enrolled in an\nactive degree program Training, Skills, Knowledge, Experience: MA degree in clinical psychology or equivalent; Extensive experience in psychological testing and assessment; ideal candidate is enrolled in doctoral study in clinical psychology an