      "title": "Student Worker",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Student Worker Student Worker No. 1010 Long Island University Brookville, New York Center for Gifted Youth Posted Aug 21, 2026 $17 an hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 an hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-exempt Application Deadline Jan 01, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Saturday\nmorning and summer program Part-time - 4 hours each Saturday for ten weeks in the fall and ten weeks in the spring. The first Saturday will be 5 hours. Full month in July 9 A.M. - 4:00 P.M. {19 days in July) Number\nof Hours per week: 4 hours fall/4 hours\nspring/ 35 hours summer. Number of Months per Year: {10\nSaturdays in the fall, 10 Saturdays in the spring, 19 days in the summer (July) Reports\nto: Headmaster and Director of the Center for Gifted Youth / Associate Dean / Dean Qualifications\nand Skills: Bright and responsible individuals who love working with\nschool age children. College education majors highly preferred {Preference\ngiven to LIU students and LIU alumni). Job Overview: Perform duties that are instructional in nature or deliver direct services to students or parents. Performance\nResponsibilities: Foster\na nurturing environment conducive to academic success and fulfillment. Provide teachers with support in the classrooms -- work under the guidance and supervision of the teacher assigned to\nthe class. Provide direct assistance to students with specific\nregard to student safety throughout the campus. Engage with students in\nactivities in the classroom under teacher supervision. Housekeeping: putting the classroom in order, passing out\nresource materials, lab equipment, art supplies and assist in classroom projects\nas assigned by the teacher. Take attendance and escort children to the\nbathroom during classroom session. Supervise and escort children from one class\nto the other until dismissal time. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to\nextending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can\ncontribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages applications from all\nqualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic\ninformation, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression,\nmarital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status,\nveteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by\napplicable local, state or federal laws. \nHiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 58 Days Since Posted 5 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
