      "title": "Federal Work-Study: Undergraduate Student: Veterinary Technology Program",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Federal Work-Study: Undergraduate Student: Veterinary Technology Program Federal Work-Study: Undergraduate Student: Veterinary Technology Program No. 3890 Long Island University Brookville, New York Vet Tech Posted Aug 21, 2026 $17 per hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 per hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline May 04, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Name of the position : Undergraduate Student: Veterinary Technology Program I s this Federal work Study : Yes Campus : Post Department Name and ID#: Therapeutic Sciences/Veterinary Technology Program Department Dean and or Director : Dean Michael Pantalon, Dr. Jean Oberg, Director Location : Life Sciences, Room 02 - Lower Level Supervisor Name : Dr. Jean Oberg Basic Function and Scope of Responsibilities: The office of the Veterinary Technology Program is seeking an undergraduate student with capacity to complete various administrative tasks and support the program's faculty with daily office operations. Duties and Principal Responsibilities: Administrative duties including strong Microsoft Office Suite skills answering phones, forwarding inquiries to appropriate areas duplicating, filing, scanning, running errands as needed, interfacing with campus departments and working with computers and emails. Outlook and Excel a plus. Applicants must be professional, punctual, reliable, highly organized, with a strong work ethic. If applicable: tutoring undergraduates, you must have a recommendation from the faculty who teaches the course. Period Of Employment : 9/26-5/27 LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunities in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 59 Days Since Posted 4 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
