    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4612": {
      "title": "PT Factulty Clinical Supervis",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU PT Factulty Clinical Supervis PT Factulty Clinical Supervis No. 4612 Long Island University Brookville, New York Psychology Doctoral Program (Post) Posted Aug 20, 2026 $30,000 stipend Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Staff Salary Range $30,000 stipend Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Feb 27, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Department of Psychology/Clinical Psychology Doctoral Program Psychological Services Center, Part-Time Clinical Faculty Supervisor The Clinical Psychology Doctoral Program and Department of Psychology at the Long Island University/Post Campus is seeking applications for a Part-Time Clinical Faculty Supervisor for the Psychological Services Center (PSC). This position is a stipend position, 16 hours per week on campus, set to begin in September 2025. Candidates must have a PsyD or PhD from an APA-accredited clinical psychology program and hold a New York license in Psychology. Responsibilities include the following: assisting the PSC Director in the development and implementation of policies and procedures, facilitating students’ professional development and training, attending PSC administrative and clinical meetings, conducting phone screenings, triaging clinical cases, coordinating clinic didactics, supervising students, and ensuring fidelity to maintaining the PSC mission. The Part-Time Clinical Faculty Supervisor also aids in the creation and maintenance of intra-departmental (i.e., the PsyD academic program), inter-departmental (i.e., LIU programs and offices), and community relationships and collaborations. Finally, the Part-Time Clinical Faculty Supervisor provides crucial on-site support for all PSC trainees during the workday and evenings when no other licensed clinical staff are available. The PSC is a training site for the PsyD Clinical Psychology Program, a dual-orientation program that trains students in cognitive-behavioral and psychodynamic therapies. The center serves children, adolescents, and adult clients from the community. The doctoral program endorses a practitioner-scholar training model and is accredited - on probation - under appeal by the American Psychological Association. Complete applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. The salary is a stipend of $30,000. To apply, submit a cover letter of interest, curriculum vitae, and complete contact information for at least three references to Frances Dalis, PsyD, LMSW, RPT-S. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunities in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 60 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Staff Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
