    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4929": {
      "title": "Head Coach - Women's Rowing",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Head Coach - Women's Rowing Head Coach - Women's Rowing No. 4929 Long Island University Brookville, New York Athletics-Rowing Posted Aug 13, 2026 $70,000 - $75,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $70,000 - $75,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Nov 13, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Position Summary: Long Island University provides a wide array of athletic opportunities on both the intercollegiate and recreational levels which will enhance and enrich the educational experience of our students, as well as provide recreational and fitness facilities and activities for the entire University community. This full-time position is responsible for oversight of all aspects of Women's Rowing program including recruiting, coaching, and counseling of student-athletes. Key Responsibilities: Oversee fiscal responsibilities pertaining to preparing, monitoring, and verifying expenditures associated with program. Provide leadership and instruction in the personal and athletic development of student athletes. Direct and coordinate the rowing staff including planning, organization, and coaching of the rowing team. Support fundraising efforts for ongoing operation of rowing program. Evaluate and implement innovations in rowing strategy and equipment. Coach and instruct student-athletes in sport-specific skills, training techniques, and strategies through preparation, practice, and competition (race strategy), providing guidance in both group and individual settings. Recruit student-athletes by identifying, evaluating, and vetting prospects, coordinating communications and visits, and collaborating with admissions and financial aid to support enrollment. Collaborate with departmental staff to support operations, ensure compliance with NCAA, NEC, and University policies. Supervise staff and direct the day-to-day activities and manages the performance of rowing staff. Lead the team’s travel planning, paperwork, budget management, and other administrative duties. Raise funds by cultivating relationships with major gift donors. Candidate should be able to motivate recruits, athletes, and alumni to support the program enthusiastically. Other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Required Qualifications: Bachelor of Science. A valid drivers license required. Strong communication, public relations, and management skills. Ability to work a flexible schedule including nights and weekends. Ability to work with a diverse campus constituency; including students, parents, coaches, faculty, staff and alumni. Preferred Qualifications: 3 to 5 years of coaching experience required, preferably on the collegiate level. Knowledge of NCAA policies and procedures preferred. About LIU Post: LIU Post campus is a scenic, historic, and scholarly campus that offers a small-school environment with the access and resources of a major metropolitan university. The University's 350+ acre campus is located on the estate of Marjorie Merriweather Post, 27 miles east of New York City on Long Island's Gold Coast. The campus houses the Lewyt College of Veterinary Medicine, the first professional School of Accountancy, an AACSB-accredited Business School, and an award-winning theater program. LIU is home to the world-renowned Tilles Center for the Performing Arts and the Shark Stadium, where supporters gather to cheer on the Sharks’ Division I athletic program. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 67 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Closing Soon Applications close on Nov 13, 2026 You Might Also Like Women’s Rowing- Assistant Coach ... #5036 Athletics-Rowing © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4991": {
      "title": "Theatre Department Work-Study Position",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Theatre Department Work-Study Position Theatre Department Work-Study Position No. 4991 Long Island University Brookville, New York Theatre Posted Aug 13, 2026 $17 an hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 an hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non- Exempt Application Deadline Jan 22, 2027 Contact Please complete online application Job Description Position Summary: The Department of Theatre and Arts Management at Long Island University Post in Brookville, NY, is currently\naccepting work-study applications for employment with the Theatre Department and the Post Theatre Company.\nHired students will work in one of the three areas listed below in support of the Post Theatre Company's 2026–\n2027 season. When applying, please indicate your area(s) of interest and describe any relevant experience. BOX OFFICE STAFF Assist with ticketing, patron services, and front-of-house operations.\nUnder the supervision of the General Manager and Box Office Managers, students staff the Post Theatre\nCompany Box Office during weekday operating hours (typically 12:00 p.m.–5:00 p.m.) and during performances\nthroughout the semester. Evening and weekend availability is required. Responsibilities: Assisting patrons with ticket sales, reservations, and customer service. Answering phones and responding to box office inquiries. Maintaining ticketing, financial, and reservation records. Assisting with lobby setup, displays, and general organization. Assisting house management during performances, including ushering, ticket scanning, concessions, and\naudience services. Following established box office procedures and assisting with opening, intermission, and closing\nresponsibilities. Reporting patron, facility, or safety concerns to the General Manager or Company Manager. PRODUCTION ASSISTANT Assist with scenery, lighting, props, painting, and production support. Under the supervision of the Technical Director and General Manager, Production Assistants support the\npreparation and execution of Post Theatre Company productions and assist in maintaining theatre facilities. Instruction in the use of tools, equipment, and construction techniques will be provided. Work may include evening and weekend hours, particularly during the two weeks leading up to each production's opening. Responsibilities: Scenic construction/installation Lighting Painting Prop building Administrative and production support General maintenance of the PTC Main Stage, Lab Theater, and other spaces. COSTUME SHOP ASSISTANT Support costume construction, maintenance, and organization. Under the supervision of the Costume Shop Supervisor, Costume Designer, and designated Costume Shop staff,\nCostume Shop Assistants. Responsibilities: Assisting with costume pulling, construction, alteration, maintenance, and strike for assigned\nproductions. Maintaining the organization and upkeep of the Costume Shop and costume collection. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunities in employment to all\nqualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU\nencourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information,\nsexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin,\nethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable\nlocal, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 67 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4978": {
      "title": "Assistant Technical Director",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Assistant Technical Director Assistant Technical Director No. 4978 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Dean-RocNation School Posted Aug 12, 2026 $50,000 - $55,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $50,000 - $55,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Nov 12, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary The Assistant Technical Director supports the daily operation and maintenance of the Roc Nation School’s technical infrastructure across studios, tech-labs, classrooms, rehearsal spaces and our Kumble Theatre. Your role will serve as an integral member of the technical operations and production team, ensuring that educational, creative, and public events are supported by reliable, professional-grade technology. Responsibilities Recording Studio & Production Technology Support Maintain and support professional recording studios and production labs. Troubleshoot A/V equipment, studio monitors, microphones, software suites, and all audio hardware. Configure, maintain, and support audio software workstations including Pro Tools, Logic Pro, Ableton Live, FL Studio, and associated plug-ins and software. Assist with equipment calibration, signal flow, and preventative maintenance. Coordinate equipment repairs, warranty service, and vendor support. Classroom & Educational Technology Provide technical support for university facilities, including technology, piano, and drum labs. Ensure all instructional spaces remain operational, organized, and fully functional for academic use. Assist faculty with classroom technology systems, software installations, and computer workstations. Support student projects, coursework, capstone productions, recording sessions, and technical demonstrations. Facilitate software deployment, updates, and license management for instructional computer labs. Train students and faculty on the safe and effective operation of university technology and production equipment. Live Sound, Theater & Event Production Support live events, showcases, recitals, theatrical productions, guest lectures, and industry events. Serve as technical support for productions and events held in Kumble Theatre, including evenings and weekends as required by the university's event schedule. Assist with venue setup, technical rehearsals, strike, and event logistics. Operate or support mixing consoles, wireless microphone systems, speaker management systems, and playback systems. Assist with livestream and hybrid event production as needed. Technical Operations Maintain inventories of audio, video, lighting, and production equipment. Perform preventative maintenance and routine inspections of technical systems. Assist with installation of new equipment, infrastructure improvements, and technology upgrades. Maintain technical documentation, equipment records, and operational procedures. Respond promptly to technical issues and service requests across university instructional and performance spaces. Minimum Qualifications 3+ years of experience supporting professional audio, AV, studio, theater, or live event environments. Strong knowledge of signal flow, audio systems, and production technology. Experience with digital audio workstations and professional recording equipment. Experience with live sound. Strong technical troubleshooting skills are important. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education, conservatory, or music school environments. Proficiency with Pro Tools and Avid products. Familiarity with Q-SYS, Crestron, Extron, or similar AV control platforms. Experience managing software licenses and computer lab environments. Desired Skills Professional recording studio operations Audio system design troubleshooting DAW support Live sound engineering Livestream and hybrid event production Software deployment and license management Project planning and documentation Faculty and student support Training and mentorship Vendor and contractor coordination LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 68 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Closing Soon Applications close on Nov 12, 2026 © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4983": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Teacher Education",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Adjunct Instructor - Teacher Education Adjunct Instructor - Teacher Education No. 4983 Long Island University Purchase, New York Teacher Education Posted Aug 12, 2026 $1000 - $1350 per credit Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Adjunct Faculty Salary Range $1000 - $1350 per credit Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Nov 12, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application. Job Description Summary & Key Responsibilities Adjunct faculty responsibilities include the preparation for, and the teaching of, one or more assigned courses. Preparation includes:  construction of an appropriate and up-to-date syllabus to be posted in the course shell(s) on the LIU learning platform at least three days prior to the start of class; a welcome letter posted in the course shell(s) at least three days prior to the start of class; submission of the syllabus to LIU Hudson at least one week prior to the start of class; attendance at Faculty Receptions/Meetings at the start of the fall and spring semesters; timely submission of grades no more than 48 hours following the last class of the semester. Successful teaching includes: sharing course content/information; engaging students in critical thinking about course content and their field of study; encouraging a breadth and depth of thinking. Successful teaching at the graduate level also demands a high degree of professionalism and the ability to support students as their courses present them with intellectual and methodological challenges. Education Requirements ABD or master’s degree holder with relevant experience and expertise in the teaching of the specific subject matter LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 68 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Application Status Closing Soon Applications close on Nov 12, 2026 © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4982": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Postdoctoral Fellow Postdoctoral Fellow No. 4982 Long Island University Brookville, New York Veterinary Biomedical Sciences Posted Aug 12, 2026 $60,000 - $65,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $60,000 - $65,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Nov 12, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary Dr. Xiaolei Tang’s laboratory at Long Island University is seeking highly motivated and qualified candidates for an open Postdoctoral Fellow position focused on the study of regulatory T cells. We welcome applications from individuals with a strong research background and a passion for advancing immunology research. Learn more about Dr. Tang’s research program: https://liu.edu/research/research-faculty-and-administration/xiaolei-tang The incumbent will investigate the role of regulatory T cells in treating autoimmune diseases, such as multiple sclerosis, rheumatoid arthritis, type 1 diabetes, and inflammatory bowel disease, using animal models and human samples. He/she will not only conduct basic research but also gain industry experience. The fellow will primarily work in the Lewyt College of Veterinary Medicine of Long Island University, a newly established veterinary medical school. Our newly renovated research laboratory is fully equipped with state-of-the-art instruments essential for daily research activities, including a Cell Culture Biosafety Cabinet, CO2 Incubator, Flow Cytometer, ImmunoSpot Analyzer, Freeze Lyophilizer, Nanoparticle Analyzer, Confocal Microscope, and Gas Chromatography. Some publications are accessible through this link:  https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/myncbi/1J5cF1V0tC4ky/bibliography/public/ Key Responsibilities Cell Culture Maintain cell culture for primary cells and cell lines. Perform assays to evaluate cell functions such as proliferation, cytokine secretion, apoptosis, and differentiation. Flow Cytometer Perform various analyses using flow cytometers, such as cell subset and cycle analyses. Molecular Biology Isolate DNA and RNA. Perform agarose gel electrophoresis, Cloning, PCR, real-time RT-qPCR, ChIP, ChIPSeq. Knockdown genes. Overexpress genes. Biochemistry Isolate and quantify proteins. Perform SDS-PAGE, western blotting, immunoprecipitation, in vitro and in vivo biochemical assays. Immunohistochemistry Prepare paraffin-embedded and cryosections. Perform histology, H&E staining, and immunohistochemistry staining. Microscopy Analyze images using bright field, fluorescence, and confocal microscopes. Spectroscopy Use UV-Vis spectroscopy and spectrophotometry to quantify DNA, RNA, and protein. Bioinformatics Design primers. Perform sequence alignment. Bulk RNA-seq and scRNA-seq. Analyze gene sequencing data using machine-learning techniques. Small Animal Handling Breed and maintain mouse colonies. Genotype for knockout and transgenic mouse models. Perform animal procedures such as isolation of intestinal crypts, intravenous/intraperitoneal/subcutaneous injections, necropsy and tissue collection, and immunohistochemistry of tissue sections. Perform luciferase imaging of live animals. Mentoring Mentor undergraduate, Doctor of Veterinary Medicine, Master's, and PhD students. Publishing Gather and interpret experimental data and prepare reports and manuscripts. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in natural science or a health-related field from a college or university of recognized standing. Background in immunology training is preferred. One year of related experience is required. Demonstrate excellent organizational skills Willing to work on multiple projects. Work effectively with other laboratory members. Willing to work effectively with other faculty, staff, and administrators as necessary. Demonstrates the ability to independently carry out significant projects critical to the university and community. Will have a solid and consistent publication record in tissue repair and/or immunology. Please submit the following with your application: Cover letter, resume, transcripts if recently graduated, personal statement, research statement, and future research plan. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 68 Days Since Posted 0 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Closing Soon Applications close on Nov 12, 2026 You Might Also Like Administrative Assistant - Office of Academic Affa... #4995 Veterinary Biomedical Sciences Post Doctoral Fellow... #4949 Veterinary Biomedical Sciences © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4981": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Position - Vocal Performance",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Adjunct Faculty Position - Vocal Performance Adjunct Faculty Position - Vocal Performance No. 4981 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Dean-RocNation School Posted Aug 12, 2026 $1000 - $1350 per credit Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Adjunct Faculty Salary Range $1000 - $1350 per credit Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Nov 12, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary The Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment at LIU invites applications from self-directed, inspiring, and motivated individuals to join this historical partnership with LIU and Roc Nation as an adjunct professor. All courses are taught in person on LIU’s Brooklyn campus. The School is seeking applications in the following disciplines: Vocal Performance. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Vocal Performance and/or Music Education with Voice emphasis required Master's degree in Vocal Performance, Vocal Pedagogy preferred, or a closely related field preferred Demonstrated success of minimum two years of prior Higher Education experience required Experience across genres (Musical theater, Jazz, R+B etc.) and pedagogical approaches A proficient level of Keyboard skills preferred Please submit the following with your application: Cover letter including a brief summary of teaching philosophy CV/Resume Link to 5-10 minute teaching sample video Contact Information for three references About the Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment Long Island University, a nationally ranked university, and Roc Nation, a preeminent global entertainment company, have engaged in a one-of- a-kind collaboration to form the Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment. The Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment’s degree programs prepare students for a wide range of careers in performance, entrepreneurship, and all aspects of music and sports management. Students engage with world-renowned professors, learn alongside visiting guest artists and lecturers, and participate in immersive internships, ensuring they graduate with both hands-on experience and a network of professional contacts. For more information about the Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment program, please visit https://liu.edu/rocnation/. About Long Island University A dynamic teaching and research university, LIU is committed to five signature research areas: Future of Business, One Health, Data Analytics, Innovative Cures, and Resilient Communities. LIU Brooklyn is situated in the vibrant, revitalized downtown Brooklyn area. It is a short walk to Brooklyn’s renowned Promenade, the new Brooklyn Bridge Riverfront Park, the Brooklyn Academy of Music, and the walkway over the Brooklyn Bridge. Nearby neighborhoods include Park Slope, Fort Greene, DUMBO, and Brooklyn Heights. Additionally, the campus is one train stop from Manhattan and all it has to offer. Established in 1926, LIU Brooklyn is one of the fastest-growing, most ethnically diverse campuses in the metropolitan area. LIU is an equal-opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender, and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 68 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Application Status Closing Soon Applications close on Nov 12, 2026 You Might Also Like Adjunct Professor - Music, Technology, Entrepreneu... #4960 Dean-RocNation School Adjunct Professor - Vocal Performance... #4961 Dean-RocNation School © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
