    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4984": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Undergraduate Admissions",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Assistant Director, Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Undergraduate Admissions No. 4984 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Admissions (Brooklyn) Posted Aug 12, 2026 $63,000 - $66,300 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $63,000 - $66,300 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Nov 12, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application. Job Description Summary Reporting to the Campus Director of Admissions, the Assistant Director of First-Year Admissions has a primary focus on first-year student recruitment, including domestic and international students, and admissions counseling. There will also be some cross-recruitment with other markets. It incorporates a full range of admissions responsibilities including establishing and strengthening a recruitment territory, representing the University to prospective students and family members, evaluating admissions applications, and contributing to the planning and implementation of admissions projects and activities. The Assistant Director is responsible for practicing good student service principles and embracing a holistic student development strategic plan. This position requires an understanding of best practices in higher education and admissions. Key Responsibilities Serve as a primary admissions recruiter for undergraduate programs at the LIU Brooklyn/Post campus. Represent Long Island University at day and evening recruitment programs and during individual recruitment visits. Prepare and deliver presentations about the university and provide prospective students with information about academic programs, admission procedures, and policy. Present to small or large groups; conduct student interviews; provide information and guidance to prospective students and their families. Complete application review for prospective applicants. Assist with various marketing campaigns, applicant file evaluation (including secondary school, GED, and college transcripts), and a variety of administrative activities, assigned. Help to enhance relationships between the High School Guidance Counselors, Academic Program Coordinators, and the community. Counsel prospective students and their families by telephone/mail/email on admission policies and procedures and other enrollment-related information Provide appropriate follow-up to all students in attendance at recruitment events while providing a high-level of customer service Review applications, assist with credit evaluation and render admission decisions in compliance with LIU’s admission policies Maintain tracking information on students in all stages, from inquiry through enrolled Maintain and document contact with admitted students via telephone, email, and mail Prepare regular year-to-date and final progress reports for the Director Represent LIU at fairs, open houses, and other recruitment events; overnight travel is required. Other duties assigned by Director of Freshman Admissions. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Experience in Admissions or a related field is highly desired. The Assistant/Associate Director must be proficient in all Microsoft Office applications, Word, Excel, Outlook, and Power Point. Previous experience using PeopleSoft and Image Now systems is preferred. The Assistant/Associate Director must possess excellent written and oral communications skills. Additionally, the Assistant/Associate Director must exhibit strong interpersonal and time management skills. Positive attitude and ability to work in a team environment is necessary. Working Conditions: This position operates in an office setting, Monday through Friday; however, evening and weekend hours are required. Travel to New York and specific region required. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 68 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Closing Soon Applications close on Nov 12, 2026 You Might Also Like Director of Pharmacy Admission... #4964 Admissions (Brooklyn) Assistant Director, First-Year Admissions ... #4966 Admissions (Brooklyn) © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
