    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4980": {
      "title": "Women's Gymnastics Assistant Coach (Full-Time)",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Women's Gymnastics Assistant Coach (Full-Time) Women's Gymnastics Assistant Coach (Full-Time) No. 4980 Long Island University Brookville, New York Athletics-General (Post) Posted Aug 12, 2026 $65,000- $70,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $65,000- $70,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Nov 12, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary The LIU Women’s Gymnastics Assistant Coach will work closely with the Head Coach to support the gymnastics program. This role involves coaching student athletes, assisting in practice planning, and contributing to the overall success of the team. Key Responsibilities Assist in the development and implementation of training programs for gymnasts at various skill levels. Conduct coaching sessions focusing on technical skills, routines, and overall performance enhancement. Help organize and lead daily practices, ensuring a safe and positive environment for all athletes. Aid in the preparation for competitions, including routine development and mental preparation. Monitor the progress of student-athletes and provide individualized feedback and support. Participate in recruitment efforts, including attending competitions and evaluating potential recruits. Foster a supportive and inclusive team culture through open communication and mentorship. Ensure compliance with NCAA regulations and university policies in all coaching activities. Assist with administrative tasks, such as scheduling, travel arrangements, and budget management. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Sports Management, Physical Education, or a related field preferred. Previous coaching experience in gymnastics, ideally at the collegiate or club level. Strong understanding of gymnastics techniques, safety protocols, and competition rules. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends. Commitment to the academic and athletic development of student-athletes. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 68 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Closing Soon Applications close on Nov 12, 2026 You Might Also Like Men’s Soccer - Lead Assistant Coach and Recruiting... #4969 Athletics-General (Post) Men’s Soccer - Assistant Coach/Player Development ... #4970 Athletics-General (Post) Men’s Soccer- Goalie Assistant Coach (Part-Time)  ... #4971 Athletics-General (Post) © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
