      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Track and Field/Cross Country - Operations Coordinator (Part Time - Post) Track and Field/Cross Country - Operations Coordinator (Part Time - Post) No. 4975 Long Island University Brookville, New York Athletics-General (Post) Posted Aug 03, 2026 $10,000-$18,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $10,000-$18,000 Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Nov 03, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Summary Long Island University (LIU) seeks a dedicated and enthusiastic Operations Coordinator to provide the Head Coach with administrative and operational support for the LIU Men’s and Women’s Track/Cross Country programs. This part-time position includes assisting with the coordination of team operations, travel, recruiting logistics, scheduling, and day to day administrative functions that contribute to a first-class student-athlete experience. This is a part-time position  (August- May ~ 20 hours per week) based on the Post campus with responsibilities supporting both the Post and Brooklyn campuses. Duties and Responsibilities Team Operations: Coordinate team travel, including itineraries, lodging, transportation, and meal planning. Assist with facility and transportation reservations/rentals. • Meet Management: Assist with home meet operations and event management. Recruiting Operations: Assist the Director of Recruiting with administrative recruiting responsibilities. Coordinate official and unofficial recruiting visits.  Prepare recruiting itineraries and campus visit schedules. Assist with maintaining recruiting databases and organizational records. Communication & Collaboration: Serve as a liaison between coaching staff and departments including Compliance, Athletic Training, Facilities, Academic Services, Equipment, Marketing, and the Business Office.  Assist in communicating 