    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4965": {
      "title": "Director, Center for Student Success & Coaching",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Director, Center for Student Success & Coaching Director, Center for Student Success & Coaching No. 4965 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Center for Student Success and Coaching-Brooklyn Posted Jul 28, 2026 $80,000 - $85,000 Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Administrative Salary Range $80,000 - $85,000 Start Date As soon as possible. FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Oct 28, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application. Job Description Position Summary The Director of the Center for Student Success & Coaching provides strategic leadership for a comprehensive, student-centered support model designed to promote academic success, persistence, belonging, wellness, and career readiness. The Director oversees integrated student support services including academic advisement, success coaching, financial wellness support, housing and residential coordination, student engagement, institutional navigation, and coordinated student care initiatives. Working collaboratively across Academic Affairs and Student Affairs, the Director develops proactive intervention strategies, assessment practices, and holistic support systems that enhance the student experience and support institutional retention and persistence goals. Key Responsibilities Provide leadership and oversight for the daily operations of the Center for Student Success & Coaching, ensuring effective delivery of integrated student support services. Develop and assess operational procedures, student support practices, and technological systems to enhance efficiency, communication, and the student experience. Supervise, mentor, and evaluate professional staff, including Success Coaches and Associate Directors, while supporting institutional recruitment, retention, and persistence goals. Collaborate closely with the Director of the Center for Student Success & Coaching at the LIU Post campus to ensure consistency in student support practices and a unified student experience across campuses. Partner with Admissions, Registrar, Academic Affairs, Student Affairs, Learning Support Services, Center for Healthy Living, Career Engagement, and other campus offices to support recruitment, enrollment, retention, and student success initiatives. Maintain a working caseload of students by providing holistic success coaching, academic advisement, career guidance, and individualized student support plans. Coordinate proactive outreach and intervention efforts for students experiencing academic, financial, behavioral, personal, or transitional challenges. Support admissions events, orientation programs, transition initiatives, and other activities that promote student engagement and successful integration into the University community. Ensure a high standard of student-centered customer service across all functional areas of the Center. Gather, analyze, and report on student success data, retention trends, utilization of services, and other key performance indicators to inform strategic planning and assessment efforts. Participate in divisional committees, campus-wide initiatives, workshops, and professional development opportunities in support of the University’s mission and student success priorities. Perform additional responsibilities and special projects as assigned by the Student Affairs Leadership Team (Associate Dean, Assistant Vice President for Financial Aid, Associate Vice President of Student Affairs and the Vice President of Student Affairs.) Functional Areas of Support & Coordination The Center for Student Success & Coaching utilizes a holistic and integrated student support model focused on student persistence, engagement, and overall success. The Director provides leadership and coordination across the following areas: Academic Success & Advisement Academic advisement and success coaching Registration support and degree progression monitoring Early alert initiatives, at risk and academic recovery planning Institutional navigation and student intervention support Financial Wellness & Student Accounts Financial aid guidance and FAFSA support Billing, payment plans, and student account navigation Financial literacy and retention-focused financial interventions Housing, Conduct, & Student Support Housing and residential student support coordination CARE referrals and student intervention support Student conduct collaboration and restorative practices Student well-being and crisis response coordination Student Engagement & Belonging Orientation and transition programming Student organizations and leadership development Campus engagement initiatives and traditions Programs designed to foster belonging and campus connection Career Readiness & Professional Development Career exploration and planning Internship and experiential learning support Career readiness initiatives Graduate and professional school preparation Specialized Student Support Services First-generation and transfer student support International student coordination Student-athlete and Honors student support collaboration Accessibility referrals and coordinated support services Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree required. Doctorate preferred. Minimum of 7–10 years of progressively responsible experience in higher education, student affairs, enrollment management, or student success leadership. Experience supervising professional staff and coordinating integrated student support services. Strong understanding of student development, retention strategies, holistic student success models, and institutional support systems. Knowledge of academic advisement, financial aid processes, student accounts, case management practices, and student intervention strategies. Excellent leadership, organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive, equitable, and student-centered practices. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 83 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Administrative Employment Type Application Status Closing Soon Applications close on Oct 28, 2026 You Might Also Like Success Coach - Financial Aid... #5016 Center for Student Success and Coaching-Brooklyn Success Coach... #4278 Center for Student Success and Coaching-Brooklyn © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
