    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4960": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor - Music, Technology, Entrepreneurship, and Production Program",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Adjunct Professor - Music, Technology, Entrepreneurship, and Production Program Adjunct Professor - Music, Technology, Entrepreneurship, and Production Program No. 4960 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Dean-RocNation School Posted Jul 24, 2026 $1000 - $1350 per credit Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Adjunct Faculty Salary Range $1000 - $1350 per credit Start Date Open until filled. FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Oct 24, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Position Summary The Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment at LIU invites applications from self-directed, inspiring, and motivated individuals to join this historic partnership between LIU and Roc Nation as an Adjunct Professor. All courses are taught in person on LIU’s Brooklyn campus. The School is currently seeking applications in the following discipline: Music, Technology, Entrepreneurship, and Production Program. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in music technology, Recording Arts, or a closely related field required; Master’s degree preferred. A minimum of two years of successful experience in a higher education setting is required. Experience across popular music genres (Pop, R&B, Hip Hop, Alternative, Electronic) Creative pedagogical approaches that support curriculum and learning outcomes Relevant industry experience in recording, mixing and/or production at a professional level A proficient level using outboard gear, consoles, and multiple DAWs including ProTools, Ableton, and Logic Please include the following with your application: Cover letter including a brief summary of teaching philosophy CV/Resume Link to 5-10 minute teaching sample video List of professional credits, if applicable Contact Information for three references Salary: $1000 - $1350 per credit About the Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment Long Island University, a nationally ranked university, and Roc Nation, a preeminent global entertainment company, have engaged in a one-of- a-kind collaboration to form the Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment. The Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment’s degree programs prepare students for a wide range of careers in performance, entrepreneurship, and all aspects of music and sports management. Students engage with world-renowned professors, learn alongside visiting guest artists and lecturers, and participate in immersive internships, ensuring they graduate with both hands-on experience and a network of professional contacts. For more information about the Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment program, please visit https://liu.edu/rocnation/. About Long Island University A dynamic teaching and research university, LIU is committed to five signature research areas: Future of Business, One Health, Data Analytics, Innovative Cures, and Resilient Communities. LIU Brooklyn is situated in the vibrant, revitalized downtown Brooklyn area. It is a short walk to Brooklyn’s renowned Promenade, the new Brooklyn Bridge Riverfront Park, the Brooklyn Academy of Music, and the walkway over the Brooklyn Bridge. Nearby neighborhoods include Park Slope, Fort Greene, DUMBO, and Brooklyn Heights. Additionally, the campus is one train stop from Manhattan and all it has to offer. Established in 1926, LIU Brooklyn is one of the fastest-growing, most ethnically diverse campuses in the metropolitan area. LIU is an equal-opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender, and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 87 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Application Status Closing Soon Applications close on Oct 24, 2026 You Might Also Like Adjunct Professor - Vocal Performance... #4961 Dean-RocNation School Adjunct Faculty Position - Vocal Performance... #4981 Dean-RocNation School © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4961": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor - Vocal Performance",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Adjunct Professor - Vocal Performance Adjunct Professor - Vocal Performance No. 4961 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Dean-RocNation School Posted Jul 24, 2026 $1000 - $1350 per credit Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Adjunct Faculty Salary Range $1000 - $1350 per credit Start Date Open until filled. FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Oct 24, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Position Summary The Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment at LIU invites applications from self-directed, inspiring, and motivated individuals to join this historical partnership with LIU and Roc Nation as an adjunct professor. All courses are taught in person on LIU’s Brooklyn campus. The School is seeking applications in the following disciplines: Vocal Performance. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Vocal Performance and/or Music Education with a concentration in Voice required; Master’s degree in Vocal Performance, Vocal Pedagogy, or a closely related field preferred. Demonstrated success of minimum two years of prior Higher Education experience required Experience across genres (Musical theater, Jazz, R+B etc.) and pedagogical approaches A proficient level of Keyboard skills preferred Please include the following with your application: Cover letter including a brief summary of teaching philosophy CV/Resume Link to 5-10 minute teaching sample video Contact Information for three references Salary:  $1000 - $1350 per credit About the Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment Long Island University, a nationally ranked university, and Roc Nation, a preeminent global entertainment company, have engaged in a one-of- a-kind collaboration to form the Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment. The Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment’s degree programs prepare students for a wide range of careers in performance, entrepreneurship, and all aspects of music and sports management. Students engage with world-renowned professors, learn alongside visiting guest artists and lecturers, and participate in immersive internships, ensuring they graduate with both hands-on experience and a network of professional contacts. For more information about the Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment program, please visit https://liu.edu/rocnation/. About Long Island University A dynamic teaching and research university, LIU is committed to five signature research areas: Future of Business, One Health, Data Analytics, Innovative Cures, and Resilient Communities. LIU Brooklyn is situated in the vibrant, revitalized downtown Brooklyn area. It is a short walk to Brooklyn’s renowned Promenade, the new Brooklyn Bridge Riverfront Park, the Brooklyn Academy of Music, and the walkway over the Brooklyn Bridge. Nearby neighborhoods include Park Slope, Fort Greene, DUMBO, and Brooklyn Heights. Additionally, the campus is one train stop from Manhattan and all it has to offer. Established in 1926, LIU Brooklyn is one of the fastest-growing, most ethnically diverse campuses in the metropolitan area. LIU is an equal-opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender, and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 87 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Application Status Closing Soon Applications close on Oct 24, 2026 You Might Also Like Adjunct Professor - Music, Technology, Entrepreneu... #4960 Dean-RocNation School Adjunct Faculty Position - Vocal Performance... #4981 Dean-RocNation School © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4625": {
      "title": "Student Worker",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Student Worker Student Worker No. 4625 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York WellnessRecreationAthletic Ctr Posted Jul 22, 2026 $17 per hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 per hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Dec 22, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description FWS Student Fitness/Concession Assistant: Brooklyn\nDepartment: Campus Recreation Campus: LIU Brooklyn Basic Function and Scope of Responsibilities:\nThis position is for the Brooklyn Steinberg Wellness Center. This position is responsible for providing\na clean, safe & welcoming environment for all users. The Building Manager works closely with the\nother Building Managers and the Director of Campus Recreation. The responsibilities of this position\ninclude enforcing safety protocols and managing all equipment to ensure equipment and machines\nare sanitized, organized, and operating properly. Fitness/Concession Attendant Responsibilities: ● Ensure the fitness area and concession stand remains clean & organized. ● Adhere to Campus Recreation University policies. ● Actively supervise the fitness center and concession stand. ● Act in a professional manner by upholding LIU Policy when involved in conflict management with\npatrons, students, & staff. ● Perform opening/closing procedures of the fitness room and concession stand. ● Display a positive and enthusiastic attitude for all patrons Training, Skills, Knowledge, Experience: Interest or field of study related to health and fitness preferred. Experience with weight room equipment, machines and/or food service preferred. Working Conditions: Flexible hours, including weekends and evenings, are required to execute the position’s role\nresponsibly. Occasional travel to/from other LIU campuses for the facilitation of trainings, meetings and\nother university functions. Materials & Equipment: Computer, fax machine, copier, phone, POS system. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in\nemployment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our\nacademic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to\nrace, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or\nexpression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military\nstatus, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is\ncontingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 88 Days Since Posted 2 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like FWS Student Worker-Lifeguard... #1862 WellnessRecreationAthletic Ctr © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
