    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4774": {
      "title": "Event Assistant - Student Worker",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Event Assistant - Student Worker Event Assistant - Student Worker No. 4774 Long Island University Brookville, New York Student Affairs-Post Posted Jul 22, 2026 $17 per hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 per hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Dec 22, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description LIU Event Assistant Job Description\nGeneral Requirements: o Open to Undergraduate and Graduate students, potential for leadership position. o Remain in good academic, financial and judicial standing at LIU. o Have and maintain a 3.0 GPA. o Be available for training upon request. o Be available to work evenings, weekends, break, as needed. Flexible schedule. o Be an excellent communicator, responsible and time-efficient, with a friendly\ndisposition. o Candidates will need to have completed two college semesters by the start date of the\nposition. Campus Directional Knowledge is Preferred. Principal Responsibilities: o Clerical to customer service and client facing duties. o Event Support May include, but not limited to the following – ensuring designated or assigned\nevent venue or facility is ready, greeting guests, hosting check-in or registration,\nconnecting hosts with service providers, managing audio visual component. o Conference/ External Rental Group Support Assist with the preparation and execution of rental group needs.\nMay include, but not limited to the following – preparing keys, completing\npaperwork, making copies, making calls, distributing pertinent information to\nthe guests, setting up rooms for guests, inspecting guest rooms, taking work\norder requests and follow-up, linen packet issuing, keeping track of check-ins\nand check-outs, troubleshooting issues, providing proper guest service. o Be responsible for enforcing all aspects of the University Code of Conduct. o Reserve Tuesday afternoons for possible staff meetings. o Other duties as assigned by Events/ Auxiliary Management Team. Dress Code: o VIP Events- Shark polo (distributed at hiring) o Black pants or skirt o Office Hours- no sweats permitted Benefits: o $17.00 per hour o Invaluable Leadership and Resume-Building Experience o Special Event Access o LIU Community Networking Opportunities LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in\nemploymentto all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our\nacademic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard\nto race, color,religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or\nexpression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or\nmilitary status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal\nlaws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 88 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. You Might Also Like Student Worker - Student Run Business... #4372 Student Affairs-Post Federal Work-study Student Worker - Concierge... #1415 Student Affairs-Post © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
