    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4959": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Honors College Assistant , Brooklyn",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Student Worker - Honors College Assistant , Brooklyn Student Worker - Honors College Assistant , Brooklyn No. 4959 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Honors Program (Brooklyn) Posted Jul 22, 2026 $17 an hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 an hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Dec 22, 2026 Contact Submit online application Job Description Position Summary: The Honors College is seeking dedicated and motivated Honors College students who have been awarded federal work-study for the position of Honors College Assistant. This role offers a unique opportunity to actively contribute to the vibrant Honors College community by providing essential support in various areas, including maintaining Honors College spaces, assisting with events and programming, managing social media presence, and aiding in admissions-related activities. The Honors College Assistant will play a key role in enhancing the overall experience of Honors scholars and promoting the Honors College's mission of academic excellence and engagement. Key Responsibilities: Honors College Spaces Manager Responsibilities: Conduct regular walkthroughs of Honors College spaces to ensure cleanliness, organization, and overall appearance. Monitor study areas, classrooms, lounges, and common spaces for maintenance concerns and report issues to Honors College staff. Ensure technology is functioning properly, including televisions, computers, printers, projectors, and other equipment. Assist with room setup and breakdown for Honors College meetings, workshops, and events. Maintain supplies and inventory, notifying staff when items need to be restocked. Organize storage areas, closets, and Honors College materials. Serve as the first point of contact for student concerns regarding Honors College facilities. Complete weekly space reports outlining completed tasks and areas requiring attention. Time commitment: This position requires a consistent weekly commitment of at least 8 \nhours, typically spread across 2–3 days per week. Honors College Social Media Intern Responsibilities: Develop and maintain a consistent posting schedule across Honors College social media platforms. Create engaging content highlighting events, student achievements, scholarships, study abroad opportunities, and Honors College initiatives. Capture photos and videos at Honors College events. Write captions, stories, and promotional content aligned with Honors College branding. Monitor social media engagement and respond to comments or messages as directed by staff. Collaborate with student leaders and staff to promote upcoming events and initiatives. Track social media analytics and provide monthly engagement reports. Maintain a professional and positive online presence representing the Honors College. Time commitment: This position requires a consistent weekly commitment of at least 8 \nhours, typically spread across 2–3 days per week. Honors College Digital Arts & Marketing Assistant Responsibilities: Design flyers, digital advertisements, social media graphics, presentations, and promotional materials for Honors College events and initiatives. Ensure all materials follow established Honors College branding guidelines. Collaborate with staff and student leaders to create marketing campaigns for programs and events. Assist in developing visual content for newsletters, websites, and recruitment materials. Update existing marketing materials as needed. Maintain organized digital files and design templates. Meet established deadlines for promotional materials to ensure timely marketing of events. Time commitment: This position requires a consistent weekly commitment of at least 8 \nhours, typically spread across 2–3 days per week. Honors College Event Operations Assistant Responsibilities: Assist with event setup, registration, hospitality, and breakdown. Welcome guests and assist students, faculty, staff, and visitors during events. Prepare materials and supplies for Honors College programs. Assist with attendance tracking and event logistics. Help distribute promotional materials and event information. Support admissions events, open houses, orientation programs, and Honors College recruitment initiatives. Serve as an ambassador for the Honors College by providing information and answering questions about Honors programs and opportunities. Time Commitment: This position requires weekend availability and flexible scheduling \nas events and opportunities arise. Availability Monday–Thursday during Common Hour \nto assist with event setup and breakdown is highly preferred. Honors College Front Desk & Administrative Assistant Responsibilities: Staff the Honors College front desk during assigned work hours. Greet students, faculty, staff, and visitors entering Honors College spaces. Monitor visitor traffic and determine the purpose of each visit (use of Honors spaces, appointments, events, meetings, etc.). Verify scheduled appointments with Honors College staff and administrators when applicable. Notify Honors College staff when students or guests arrive for scheduled meetings. Assist students with basic questions regarding Honors College policies, events, requirements, and resources, referring more complex inquiries to appropriate staff members. Maintain visitor sign-in procedures and attendance records as directed. Assist with filing, document organization, data entry, and record maintenance. Maintain organization of the front desk area and administrative workspaces. Monitor office supply inventory and notify staff when supplies need replenishing. Assist with distributing Honors College materials, promotional items, and event information. Support Honors College staff with administrative projects and special assignments. Provide exceptional customer service and contribute to a welcoming Honors College environment. Time Commitment: This position requires a consistent weekly commitment of at least 10 \nhours, typically spread across 3-4 days per week. Education Requirements : LIU student enrolled in an active degree program Training, Skills, Knowledge, Experience : Must be an active Honors College student currently enrolled in classes. Should have been awarded federal work-study as part of their financial aid package. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal. Familiarity with social media platforms and content creation is a plus. Enthusiasm for engaging with fellow Honors students and contributing to a dynamic academic community. Reliable and punctual, with a positive and proactive attitude. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunities in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 89 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
