nt initiatives. Serve as an ambassador for the Honors College by providing information and answering \nquestions about Honors programs and opportunities. Honors College Front Desk & Administrative Assistant \nResponsibilities: Staff the Honors College front desk during assigned work hours. Greet students, faculty, staff, and visitors entering Honors College spaces. Monitor visitor traffic and determine the purpose of each visit (use of Honors spaces, \nappointments, events, meetings, etc.). Verify scheduled appointments with Honors College staff and administrators when \napplicable. Notify Honors College staff when students or guests arrive for scheduled meetings. Assist students with basic questions regarding Honors College policies, events, \nrequirements, and resources, referring more complex inquiries to appropriate staff \nmembers. Maintain visitor sign-in procedures and attendance records as directed. Assist with filing, document organization, data entry, and record maintenance. Maintain organization of the front desk area and administrative workspaces. Monitor office supply inventory and notify staff when supplies need replenishing. Assist with distributing Honors College materials, promotional items, and event \ninformation. Support Honors College staff with administrative projects and special assignments. Provide exceptional customer service and contribute to a welcoming Honors College environment. Education Requirements : LIU student enrolled in an active degree program Training, Skills, Knowledge, Experience : Must be an active Honors College student currently enrolled in classes. Should have been awarded federal work-study as part of their financial aid package. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal. Familiarity with social media platforms and content creation is a plus. Enthusiasm for engaging with fellow Honors students and contributing to a dynamic academic\ncommunity. Reliable and punctual, with a positive and proactive attitude. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunities in\nemployment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our\nacademic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard\nto race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or\nexpression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or\nmilitary status, age, disability, or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal\nlaws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 89 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
