      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Student Worker Student Worker No. 4035 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Performing Arts Department Posted Jun 26, 2026 $17 per hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 per hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-exempt Application Deadline Apr 29, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Title: Student Worker Overall Summary: Assists with managing student access to studio spaces after regular work hours. Responsibilities: The Student Worker will be available up to three days per week from 6:00pm-10:00pm to provide BFA students with access to rehearsal studios in the Humanities and Pratt Buildings. Exact hours will be specified by the BFA Acting Department Director. The Student Worker must be available on an on-call basis during their specified hours. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regards to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 115 Days Since Posted 4 Positions Available Work Study Student Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
