    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4942": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor - Doctor of Physical Therapy Program",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Adjunct Professor - Doctor of Physical Therapy Program Adjunct Professor - Doctor of Physical Therapy Program No. 4942 Long Island University Brookville, New York Physical Therapy Posted Jun 26, 2026 $1,000 - $1,350 per credit Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Adjunct Faculty Salary Range $1,000 - $1,350 per credit Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Exempt Application Deadline Dec 31, 2026 Contact Complete online application Job Description Position Summary: The School of Health Professions at Long Island University seeks a licensed physical therapist or \nother doctorly-prepared health professional who have the needed expertise to teach specific \ncourses within the DPT program. A doctoral degree is required and prior teaching experience is \npreferred. The program is housed on LIU’s historic, 330-acre Brookville campus. Class schedule is \nsomewhat flexible, depending on the specific course. Key Responsibilities: Develop and teach assigned courses or serve as secondary lab instructor, depending on the \nneeds of the program Utilize LIU’s Learning Management System (LMS) to post required course materials Assess student learning and post course grades in a timely manner Mentor entry-level DPT students as needed Be available to meet with accreditation visitors, when requested Qualifications: An earned doctoral degree in one’s professional discipline; Active license to practice physical therapy (or another health care discipline for specific \ncourses such as Pharmacology) in the State of New York; Strong communication and teaching skills Ability to utilize basic computer technology in the classroom About LIU Post LIU Post campus is a scenic, historic, and\nscholarly campus that offers a small-school environment with the access and\nresources of a major metropolitan university. The University's 350+ acre campus\nis located on the estate of Marjorie Merriweather Post, 27 miles east of New\nYork City on Long Island's Gold Coast. The campus houses the Lewyt College of\nVeterinary Medicine, the first professional School of Accountancy, an\nAACSB-accredited Business School, and an award-winning theater program. LIU is home\nto the world-renowned Tilles Center for the Performing Arts and the Shark\nStadium, where supporters gather to cheer on the Sharks’ Division I athletic\nprogram. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in \nemployment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our \nacademic community.  LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to \nrace, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or \nexpression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military \nstatus, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is \ncontingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 115 Days Since Posted 1 Positions Available Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
