    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4551": {
      "title": "Adjunct Assistant Professor - Business Administration",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Adjunct Assistant Professor - Business Administration Adjunct Assistant Professor - Business Administration No. 4551 Long Island University Brookville, New York Business Administration Posted Mar 13, 2026 $1,000-$1,350 per credit Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Adjunct Faculty Salary Range $1,000-$1,350 per credit Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline May 31, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Job Title: Adjunct Faculty – School of Business Location: LIU Post Department: Business Position Summary: The Business Department at LIU Post invites applications for Adjunct Assistant/Associate Professors with a strong academic background and professional experience. We are particularly interested in candidates qualified to design and teach both undergraduate and graduate-level courses in Marketing, International Business, Finance, General Management, and Organizational Behavior. Key Responsibilities: • Design and deliver high-quality coursework in line with program objectives. • Develop course syllabi and communicate expectations clearly to students, establishing a strong student-instructor contract. • Recommend appropriate textbooks and learning resources. •F acilitate student learning and engagement to ensure achievement of course outcomes. • Participate in learning outcomes assessment initiatives, including analyzing results and implementing changes to enhance student success. • Design, administer, and assess student projects, exams, and experiential learning activities. • Maintain regular office hours to support students academically and professionally, including internship and career guidance. • Submit required documentation punctually, including syllabi (due two weeks before the semester begins), final grades (within 24 hours of semester close), graded exams, and grade changes. • Respond promptly to university requests related to accreditation, data reporting, and compliance, such as submitting current CVs, completing AACSB surveys, and completing mandatory training (e.g., sexual harassment prevention). • Perform additional duties as assigned within the scope of the role. Required Qualifications: 1. Master’s degree (minimum) in a relevant field, with substantial professional experience. 2. Proven expertise aligned with teaching assignments in Marketing, International Business, Finance, General Management, or Organizational Behavior. 3. Willingness to undergo training to maintain instructional quality and comply with institutional or governmental standards. 4. Ability to teach both in-person and online, with proficiency in relevant instructional technologies. 5. Use of an LIU-issued email address as the primary mode of communication with students and University personnel. LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States. Back to All Jobs Quick Facts 219 Days Since Posted 4 Positions Available Adjunct Faculty Employment Type Application Status Accepting Applications This position is currently accepting applications. © 2026 Long Island University - Human Resources HR@liu.edu An error has occurred. This application may no longer respond until reloaded. An unhandled exception has occurred. See browser dev tools for details. Reload 🗙"
    },
    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/4718": {
      "title": "Student Worker/Tutor for Humanities, Natural Science, Business/ Finance",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Student Worker/Tutor for Humanities, Natural Science, Business/ Finance Student Worker/Tutor for Humanities, Natural Science, Business/ Finance No. 4718 Long Island University Brookville, New York Learning Support Center (ARC) Posted Mar 13, 2026 $17 per hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 per hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Aug 27, 2027 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Name of the position: Student Worker/Tutor Is this a Federal Work Study position? Yes Campus: Post Description: CAMPUS TUTORS in THE LEARNING CENTER for Tutoring Program Fall 2025 – Spring 2026 Department Name: The Learning Center Department’s Dean and/or Director: Marie Fatscher Location: Building and Floor: Library Main Floor Supervisor: Name: Marie Fatscher Title: Director of Learning Center Purpose or role of the position within the organization\n(Basic Function and Scope of Responsibilities): Help students understand course material; prepare for exams; help with time management, organizational/planning skills and study strategies. Need students with a strong background in core classes: English, Philosophy, Political Science, History, Psychology, laboratory science, Math, Economics, Accounting and Finance. Minimum cum gpa of 3.2 and faculty or department chair recommendation required. Duties and Principal Responsibilities: Work up to 12 hours per week in The Learning Center – located on the main floor of the Library. Education Requirements: LIU student enrolled in an\nactive degree program, Must have 3.2 gpa and faculty or department chair recommendation for the courses you want to tutor Training, Skills, Knowledge, Experience: *All student candidates must complete an employment application and submit an updated resume.* Email: marie.fatscher@liu.edu Rate of Pay : minimum hourly rate 