      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Roc Nation Student Worker Roc Nation Student Worker No. 3459 Long Island University Brooklyn, New York Dean-RocNation School Posted Apr 28, 2025 $17 per hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Work Study Student Salary Range $17 per hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-Exempt Application Deadline Oct 31, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Name of the position: Student Worker Is this a Federal Work Study position? Yes Classification of the position: Other Description : Roc Nation Student Coordinators Campus: Brooklyn Department Name and ID#: LIU Roc Nation Department’s Dean and/or Director: Matthew Caballero, Assistant Dean Location: Building and Floor: Pratt Room 614 Supervisor: Name: Matthew Caballero, Assistant Dean Title: Dean Purpose or role of the position within the organization (Basic Function and Scope of Responsibilities): The LIU Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment is in search of Student Coordinators to work with School leadership. Duties and Principal Responsibilities: Assist in capturing, editing, and promoting content; Assist in planning and managing events; Assist with reports, spreadsheets, and recruitment research; Attend open houses and lead student tours and speaking engagements; Greet incoming guests; Answer office phone and directing calls as needed; Assist with making copies, scanning, and filing documents for all Department Staff and Faculty; Organizing the department (books, documents, restocking shelves and equipment with new supplies, etc.); and other responsibilities as determined by the supervisor. Education Requirements: LIU student enrolled in an active degree program Training, Skills, Knowledge, Experience: Rate of Pay : minimum hourly rate Period of employment: Begin Date: 9/4/2024 End Date: 5/9/2025 Evaluation procedures and schedules: Student Workers will have monthly meetin