    "https://jobs.liu.edu/job_details/3177": {
      "title": "Part-time Staff - Bartender",
      "description": "LIU Job Opportunities Skip to main content JOBS.LIU.EDU Jobs at LIU Part-time Staff - Bartender Part-time Staff - Bartender No. 3177 Long Island University Brookville, New York Tilles Concessions Posted Jun 06, 2024 $20 an hour Apply Now Save Job Share Job Details Job Type Staff Salary Range $20 an hour Start Date As soon as possible FLSA Status Non-exempt Application Deadline Dec 31, 2026 Contact Please submit an online application Job Description Basic Functions and Scope of Responsibilities Non\nStudent Bartender is responsible for ensuring an excellent guest drinking\nexperience. They will be able to create classic and innovative drinks exceeding\ncustomers’ needs and expectations. Will need to lift up to 25lbs in boxes. Principal\nResponsibilities The responsibilities of the Bar Tender\ninclude but are not limited to: Prepare\nalcoholic or non-alcoholic beverages for patrons Interact\nwith customers, take orders and serve drinks Mix\ningredients to prepare cocktails Check\npatron’s identification and confirm it meets the legal drinking age Restock\nand replenish bar inventory and supplies night of show (alongside the Bar Back) Stay\nguest focused and nurture an excellent guest experience Keeping\nup with fast paced service for pre-show and intermission for theatrical events Other duties as necessary LIU is an equal opportunity employer. LIU is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community.  LIU encourages applications from all qualified individuals without regards to race, color, religion, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability or any other basis protected by applicable local, state or federal laws.  Hiring is contingent on eligibility to work in the United States